window.LUNA_CHAPTERS=(window.LUNA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":151,"title":"Chapter 151 Teaching Her to Swim Again","paragraphs":["\"Don’t do anything stupid,\" Alpha Sebastian warned as he dropped Isabella off.","The moment she got out, he spun the car around.","His destination: Southridge Estates.","He wasn’t going to the villa he’d leased at Number Eleven. He was going to Number Twenty, the house Beta Jordan had told him belonged to Eira.","He had no idea she was actually living at Number Nine.","When Alpha Sebastian pulled up to Number Twenty, the lights were on. The yard was manicured, the gate stood open.","Alpha Sebastian walked up to the front door. He stopped beneath the security camera, a discreet motion sensor blinking red in the corner.","He rang the bell.","Once.","Twice.","No answer.","\"Eira, I know you’re in there.\" His voice, usually a low growl of command, softened into a desperate plea. \"Please. Just talk to me. Whatever went wrong between us, we can fix it. I swear it.\"","He paused, the silence stretching, thick and heavy. Then he tried again.","\"Starting this month, every cent I earn—every damn dollar—goes to you. You handle the accounts. You make the the decisions. It’s all yours, Eira. Just come out.\"","The house remained silent. Even the wind seemed to hold its breath.","Alpha Sebastian’s hand fell to his side, a tremor running through his fingers.","\"It’s been so long since we sat down. Really talked. Shared a meal. I miss that, Eira. I miss us.\"","His voice grew rough, edged with a frustration he couldn’t hide.","\"And Serena...\" He ran a hand through his hair. \"There’s nothing between us. It was a mistake. Just pack gossip. I swear on my Alpha blood.\"","He stepped closer to the door, his fist hovering an inch from the polished wood.","\"If you want me to stay away from her, I will. Whatever you want. Just open the door.\"","Only the faint hum of the city answered him.","But someone was listening.","The moment the doorbell rang, a secure feed popped up on Mrs. Jones’s tablet.","She watched Alpha Sebastian’s face, etched with raw desperation, watched him make one frantic promise after another. Her lips thinned.","\"Too little, too late, you fool,\" she muttered.","She forwarded the recording to her Alpha.","--","Meanwhile, Alpha Killian and the others had just returned from the yacht party. Lila had gone one glass of wine too far and was leaning against Eira, cuddling her like an oversized puppy.","\"Easy, lightweight,\" Alpha Killian muttered.","Lila yawned. \"You’re jealous. Too bad I’m the wrong gender. That’s why you can’t be Eira’s best friend.\"","Alpha Killian gave her a flat look. He just stared at Eira. Best friend? Not even close.","He glanced at Eira. She had been quiet throughout dinner, her eyes closed as if she were trying to shut out the entire world. Alpha Sebastian had a real talent for ruining everyone’s evening.","Alpha Killian’s phone buzzed. Mrs. Jones had sent him the security footage.","He played the clip without sound.","\"Sebastian?\" Eira opened her eyes and looked at the screen.","Alpha Killian handed her the phone and offered her one of his wireless earbuds. He kept the other in his ear.","Alpha Sebastian’s voice filled the quiet ride home.","Alpha Killian watched Eira’s expression change. Her brows drew together for a moment, then her face went blank again. He could not tell what she was thinking.","\"Well?\"","Eira removed the earbud and returned it to him.","\"Not worth my time. I’m meeting his mother tomorrow.\"","Alpha Killian already knew about the meeting. Lila had mentioned it earlier.","Eira wasn’t going to fall for another round of empty promises. She had watched Alpha Sebastian carry Serena away on the yacht and quietly recorded the whole thing. No tears. No scene. Just a phone held steady in her hand.","That kind of self-control made Alpha Killian uneasy. He knew Alpha Sebastian had built those walls, scars deep enough to make Eira distrust every hand reaching for her.","The thought stayed with Alpha Killian long after the car pulled into the driveway.","That night, he sent his mother a few messages asking for help.","--","Morning came early.","Eira slipped out from under the blankets without waking Lila, got ready, and went downstairs.","Mrs. Jones was already at the stove.","\"Morning, Eira. Breakfast is almost ready. Figured you’d be up before Lila. That girl sleeps like the dead.\"","\"Thanks, Mrs. Jones.\" Eira took a seat.","Mrs. Jones set down a plate of sliced fruit. \"So, when are you moving out of here? We’ve had some guy hanging around Southridge lately. He keeps standing outside an empty villa and yelling your name.\"","Southridge Estates did not attract that kind of trouble.","Mrs. Jones was obviously talking about someone specific. The only person connected to Eira who would stand outside a stranger’s house shouting for her was Alpha Sebastian.","\"You mean Sebastian.\"","Mrs. Jones grinned. \"Nothing gets past you.\"","\"How did he even get into Southridge?\" Eira asked, surprised. Security here was tight.","\"He came to pay the rent,\" Mrs. Jones said, then quickly covered her mouth. \"Oops. I probably shouldn’t have said that.\"","Eira raised an eyebrow.","\"He rented a place here. Sterling developed the whole community, so he’s basically putting money straight into Alpha Killian’s pocket.\"","Eira nodded. \"And why was he yelling outside someone else’s villa?\"","\"It’s empty. No one lives there.\" Mrs. Jones lowered her voice. \"Alpha Killian told me to send him there so he wouldn’t bother you.\"","Her eyes sparkled with amusement.","\"Alpha Killian really does worry about you. You must mean a lot to him.\"","Eira took a sip of milk and gave her a flat look.","\"Did you get that line from the romance novel you were listening to last night?\"","Mrs. Jones gasped. \"How did you know?\"","\"You had the volume turned all the way up.\"","Mrs. Jones froze.","\"Right. My AirPods must be broken. I’ll buy new ones.\"","After breakfast, Eira called Luna Margaret.","\"I’m free today. We can meet in person.\"","Luna Margaret agreed immediately. They set a time for half an hour later.","The moment they sat down, Luna Margaret got straight to the point.","\"If I help you get the evidence, are you taking Serena to court or trying to settle this privately? Because if you’re suing her, I’m out.\"","Eira looked at her calmly.","\"You’re not doing this for me. You want to recover your son’s money.\"","Luna Margaret’s jaw tightened, but she didn’t back down.","\"Court or settlement?\"","\"Court.\"","\"Absolutely not.\" Luna Margaret pushed back her chair.","\"One hundred million dollars,\" Eira said, cutting through Luna Margaret’s protest. \"That’s what Sebastian lost. Minimum. A private settlement won’t get you even a fraction of that back. Sebastian will step in, bury the evidence, and make sure Serena walks away with most of it.\"","\"If you want every dollar returned, court is the only way.\""]},{"number":152,"title":"Chapter 152 A Hundred Million on the Table","paragraphs":["\"That much?\" Luna Margaret sank back in her chair.","Eira did not blink. \"Sebastian has always earned well, especially after the Carter Group investment. One successful product launch could bring in huge bonuses and stock dividends. He had the money to burn.\"","The wife had not known. Neither had his parents or his sister. Only Serena knew. She had not just known about the money. She had bled him dry.","Luna Margaret’s face flushed. \"Is there really no way to handle this without going to court? We can’t have a scandal.\"","\"I’m naming Serena in the lawsuit. Sebastian won’t be the defendant.\" Eira raised an eyebrow. \"So what are you worried about? \"","\"What am I worried about?\" Luna Margaret lowered her voice. \"Your lawsuit will drag the Hale name through the mud. Sebastian just lost a major contract, and the shareholders are already looking for someone to blame. Add a scandal involving his mistress, and they’ll tear him apart. \"","Eira leaned back.\"Think carefully. We’re talking about one hundred million dollars.\"","\"And what does that money have to do with us?\" Luna Margaret shot back. \"If Serena has to return it, the money goes to you. You and Sebastian are already divorced. Recovered assets belong to you, not the Hale family. \"","Eira studied her.\"So how much of the Hale family’s share do you want?\"","Luna Margaret’s eyes sharpened.","\"Seventy-thirty. Seventy percent goes to us. That was my son’s money in the first place. If you’re serious, I’ll find the evidence myself.\"","She sounded confident, full of the righteous fury of a mother defending her son. Luna Margaret believed she was the only person who could uncover proof of Sebastian and Serena’s affair. She also assumed Eira would not want to do the dirty work herself.","She was wrong. Eira could get the evidence. It was only a matter of time. She had no intention of rewarding Luna Margaret’s greed.","\"Then I’ll find another way.\"","Eira stood.","Luna Margaret froze.","\"Wait.\" She gave in. \"Fifty-fifty.\"","Eira remained standing.","\"That’s more than fair,\" Luna Margaret snapped. \"Don’t push your luck.\"","\"You’re the one who needs to think this through,\" Eira said calmly. \"If I don’t sue, Serena keeps the money. You get nothing, and I get nothing. As Sebastian’s former spouse, I can claim a portion of assets acquired during our marriage. What legal right does the Hale family have to the money Serena took from Sebastian directly?\"","Luna Margaret opened her mouth, but no answer came.","What right did they have? Alpha Sebastian had handed the money to Serena himself.","Luna Margaret drained her glass of water and finally forced out, \"Sixty-forty.\"","Silence settled between them.","Three minutes later, Luna Margaret slammed her hand on the table, a final, frustrated surrender. \"Fine. Seventy percent for you. Thirty percent for us.\"","Eira nodded. \"Deal.\"","\"We’re putting it in writing. I want everything in black and white, or you’ll cut me out later.\"","\"Of course. But not until you deliver usable evidence. If your proof falls apart after I’ve already secured my own, you won’t get paid.\"","\"You’re a shark.\" Luna Margaret glared at her. \"How did I never see that before?\"","Eira almost smiled.She had always been careful with money.","Luna Margaret left in a fury to find a cab.","Eira sat back down, took a sip of water, and enjoyed the silence.","It lasted less than a minute.","A shadow fell over her table.","\"What were you and my mother talking about?\" Isabella demanded. \"I heard something about money. What money?\"","Eira looked up. \"Where were you?\"","\"You’re the one hiding things.\" Isabella dropped into the chair across from her. \"I was sitting right over there.\"","She had followed Luna Margaret into the café and slipped into a corner booth. Unfortunately, she had been too far away to hear much. The only thing she had clearly caught was her mother’s shocked cry, \"That much?\"","She had failed to find Serena on the yacht the night before, and Alpha Sebastian had driven her home before she could get any answers. She still had no idea where Serena lived.","\"Is this about the money my brother lent Serena?\" Isabella leaned across the table.","\"Lent?\" Eira leaned back. \"Who told you that? Sebastian?\"","\"My brother did.\"","Eira’s expression stayed calm. \"Then he lied to you.\"","Isabella’s face hardened. \"You weren’t exactly more important to him than Serena.\"","\"He doesn’t matter to me anymore.\"","Isabella scoffed. \"Then why did you drag out the divorce for so long?\"","Eira ignored the bait.","\"That money wasn’t a loan,\" she said. \"It was Sebastian’s slush fund for Serena. He gave her whatever she wanted, while you got nothing.\"","The words hit hard. Isabella slapped both hands on the table.","\"Do you know where she lives?\"","Eira raised her brows. \"She never invited you over? The penthouse Sebastian bought for her is nicer than your place.\"","\"Where?\" Isabella demanded, her voice tight.","\"The Celestia Residences. I can take you there.\"","Alpha Killian’s Sterling Group records had given Eira the building, floor, and unit number.","The moment Isabella heard the name, she understood why her mother had nearly passed out.","\"Take me. Now.\"","\"Gladly.\"","The Celestia Residences allowed only residents and approved guests inside. Fortunately, Sterling Group had developed the building.","Eira sent Lila a quick message: Meet me at Celestia. ASAP. Big trouble.","Lila arrived within minutes, clearly delighted by the promise of chaos. She owned several units in the building and got them through the lobby without difficulty.","But getting into Serena’s actual apartment still required individual keycards.","\"Call Serena,\" Eira told Isabella. \"Tell her Sebastian is looking for her. She’ll come down.\"","Isabella pulled out her phone, still furious.","\"She ignored me last night and made me look like an idiot.\"","\"She was busy,\" Lila said sweetly. \"She was doing a swan dive off a yacht.\"","Isabella stared at her, but the call connected before she could ask what that meant.","\"Serena?\" Isabella said. \"My brother and I are downstairs, but we don’t have a keycard. Can you come let us in?\"","Serena did not suspect a thing.","She agreed to come down at once.","Eira and Lila exchanged a look.","Showtime."]},{"number":153,"title":"Chapter 153 Two Cats in an Alley","paragraphs":["Lila pulled Eira behind a neatly trimmed hedge near the flower beds. They crouched beside a mature oak, using its broad trunk as cover while they watched the lobby entrance.","\"What did you say to Isabella?\" Lila whispered. \"She looks ready to tear Serena apart.\"","\"I compared her to Serena and asked which one Sebastian had actually spoiled.\"","Lila blinked. \"You compared his sister to his mistress?\"","\"Isabella thinks she should always come first with her brother. Even his mate shouldn’t outrank her.\"","\"Family is important,\" Lila said, shaking her head. \"But once a male has a mate, that mate becomes his immediate family. His sister doesn’t get to compete with her.\"","Eira touched her arm and nodded toward the lobby.","\"There she is.\"","Serena stepped outside. When she saw Isabella waiting alone, her brows pulled together.","\"Isabella? Where’s your brother?\"","\"He didn’t come.\" Isabella’s eyes moved over Serena’s face, designer clothes, and handbag. Everything about her looked expensive.","Serena noticed the scrutiny and felt a flicker of unease.","\"If Sebastian isn’t here, why did you ask me to come down?\" she asked, smoothing her hair behind one ear. She still had no idea the Hales had discovered where Alpha Sebastian’s money had gone.","\"All these years, Sebastian gave you the money, didn’t he?\" Isabella asked. \"Not Eira. You.\"","Serena went still.","How did she find out so quickly?","She forced a smile. \"That’s not true. Who told you? Eira?\"","The moment she mentioned Eira, Isabella’s expression changed.","\"I knew it,\" Serena continued quickly. \"Eira has always tried to turn this family against me. She’s probably been filling your head with lies.\"","\"My mother told me!\" Isabella shouted. \"Everyone knows. I was the last person to find out!\"","Serena’s face drained of color.","\"So Sebastian spent everything on you?\" Isabella demanded.","\"That isn’t what happened. Let me explain.\"","\"And you used his money to buy gifts for our whole family!\"","Isabella swung the diamond-studded handbag from her arm and slammed it into Serena’s shoulder.","Serena stumbled back.","\"Isabella, stop. Let me explain!\"","\"I don’t want excuses. I want my brother’s money back!\"","She swung the bag again. Serena raised her arms to protect her head, but the heavy bag struck her temple. Her skin flushed red, and a bruise began to form.","Lila stared from behind the hedge.\"Wow. Isabella can really throw down.\"","Eira nodded. \"She’s no pushover.\"","Across the courtyard, Serena finally snapped.","When Isabella paused to catch her breath, Serena shoved herself upright.","\"That’s enough!\" she yelled. \"You came at me before checking the facts. How can you be this reckless?\"","Lila’s eyes widened. \"She’s already trying to turn this around.\"","\"Serena never admits anything unless the evidence is right in front of her,\" Eira said.","Lila leaned closer. \"Did you bring the records?\"","Eira pulled a thin folder from her bag.","\"Not everything. This is enough to get her attention.\"","Lila’s face lit up. \"You actually brought them?\"","Eira gave her a calm look.","\"I never meet with the Hale family without bringing proof.\"","Lila reached for the folder, but Eira held on to it.","\"I’ll give it to Isabella. I don’t want you getting clipped by accident. She swings like a wrecking ball.\"","\"Then you’re not going over there alone.\"","Serena was still yelling at Isabella, trying to assert some kind of dominance, when Eira and Lila stepped from behind the oak. They crossed the courtyard at an easy pace.","The moment Serena saw the folder in Eira’s hand, all the color drained from her face.","\"Eira.\" Her glare sharpened. \"You put Isabella up to this, didn’t you? What lies have you been spreading about me now?\"","Eira ignored her and handed the folder to Isabella.","\"Read it. You’re not the only one who knows.\"","Isabella flipped through the documents. Her hands began to shake.","\"Three hundred thousand dollars a month,\" she said. \"It’s all here.\"","She looked up at Serena, her face twisted with rage.","\"You shameless little liar!\"","Serena took a step back. \"Isabella, listen to me. This isn’t what you think.\"","\"You stole my brother’s money!\"","Isabella grabbed Serena by the hair and slapped her across the face.","Serena cried out and tried to pull free, but Isabella was stronger and completely out of control. Another slap cracked through the courtyard.","Eira and Lila immediately stepped back.","\"Is that really Isabella?\" Lila asked.","\"This time, she thinks she’s the one in the right,\" Eira said. She pulled Lila farther away. \"Once Isabella believes she has the moral high ground, nobody can stop her.\"","The two women stumbled and went down in a tangled heap. Isabella ended up sitting across Serena’s legs, swinging the handbag in her hand and shouting insults between every hit.","\"She really does love money,\" Lila muttered.","\"She learned it from Luna Margaret,\" Eira said. \"Isabella just took it to another level.\"","The noise brought security running.","Two guards pulled the women apart. Serena’s hair was a mess, her dress was twisted, and dust streaked one side of her clothes. She covered her face with both hands.","Her cheeks were mostly untouched, but her hands and neck were bright red.","Lila winced. \"Lots of hits. Terrible aim.\"","\"Ma’am, do you want us to call the police?\" one of the guards asked Serena.","Serena shook her head.","She still had something to lose. If the police got involved, the financial records could become public, and Isabella could tell Alpha Sebastian everything.","She lowered her hands and forced a calm expression.","\"Isabella, you’ve made your point. Go home, and I won’t tell your brother about this.\"","Isabella spat onto the pavement.","\"Like I care what you tell him.\"","Lila glanced at Eira, clearly enjoying the chaos.","\"What do you think would happen if Sebastian showed up right now?\"","Eira gave her a knowing look.","Then she took out her phone, snapped a picture of Serena’s disheveled appearance and Isabella’s furious expression, and sent it to Alpha Sebastian.","The caption read:","Your sister and your favorite woman are throwing hands at the Celestia Residences."]},{"number":154,"title":"Chapter 154 The Slap That Ended Everything","paragraphs":["Eira thought the caption was accurate enough.","Alpha Sebastian fixated on one phrase: your favorite woman.","His expression darkened as he zoomed in on the photo. Isabella and Serena both looked like they had just come out of a back-alley brawl.","A few minutes later, he called Serena.","\"Did Isabella attack you? Are you hurt?\"","\"Sebastian...\" Serena’s voice trembled. She sounded close to tears. \"I’m fine. Just a little sore. Isabella didn’t mean it. And Eira is here too.\"","The last part was enough to set him off.","Eira put her up to this.","He already knew Eira was there. She had sent him the photo herself.","He had gone through half a dozen phone numbers lately, and she had blocked every one within a day. The latest number still worked, though he was not sure that counted as progress.","\"I’m on my way.\"","His voice was tight with exhaustion and concern.","As soon as the call ended, he opened a new message to Eira.","Stay at the Celestia Residences. Wait for me.","The message failed to send.","Blocked again.","Alpha Sebastian stared at the screen, his jaw clenched.","He had not even managed to repair things with Eira, and now Isabella had made everything worse by attacking Serena.","What the hell was wrong with his sister?","--","Isabella overheard Alpha Sebastian’s call and decided she needed some backup of her own. She pulled out her phone and called Luna Margaret.","Luna Margaret and Alpha Sebastian arrived within minutes, their faces grim.","When they reached the lobby, only Serena and Isabella were still there. Eira and Lila were long gone.","Alpha Sebastian let out a quiet breath.","Serena’s eyes filled with tears when she saw him. She started toward him, but Luna Margaret’s cold stare stopped her dead in her tracks.","Luna Margaret turned to her daughter.","\"What were you thinking, starting a public brawl?\"","Isabella planted her hands on her hips. \"What else was I supposed to do? Three hundred thousand dollars a month, Mom. Every month. He’s been bankrolling that bitch.\"","\"Isabella.\" Alpha Sebastian’s expression darkened. \"Watch your mouth.\"","Luna Margaret spun toward him. \"Don’t you dare take Serena’s side again. She’s not pack.\"","Not long ago, Luna Margaret had called Serena sweetheart. Now she was treating her like a stranger.","Alpha Sebastian walked over to Serena. A bruise was already forming on her forehead, and red marks covered her neck and hands.","\"Are you hurt anywhere else?\"","\"My stomach and my back.\" Serena tried to move, then winced. Isabella had knocked her down and hit her hard enough that everything ached.","Alpha Sebastian’s brow furrowed.","\"We’re going to the hospital,\" he said. \"Both of you. Get checked out.\"","He looked at Isabella.","\"After the doctor clears you, you and I are going to talk about the money.\"","\"What money?\" Isabella snapped. \"What have I ever cost you? Did I get three hundred thousand dollars a month? You’re my brother. Even if you gave me that much, I’d have every right to it.\"","\"Enough.\" Luna Margaret caught Isabella by the hand. \"We’re not fighting each other. We stick together. Now let the doctors examine you. We need to make sure there’s no serious damage.\"","Then she looked at Serena. Her expression held no warmth.","\"And you and I will have a conversation later.\"","Serena’s stomach dropped.","She had spent years trying to win over the Hale family. Once they accepted her, she had believed Alpha Sebastian would eventually marry her. Eira had never been close to them anyway.","Now everything had changed.","Alpha Sebastian was searching for Eira, while his family had turned against Serena.","Alpha Sebastian headed for the exit.","\"Come on. We’re going to the hospital.\"","He did not offer Serena his arm. He did not carry her. He barely looked at her.","His eyes kept sweeping the grounds for Eira.","Serena remained where she was.","\"Sebastian, I don’t think I can walk. Could you carry me?\"","\"Unbelievable,\" Isabella muttered.","Serena truly was in pain, but Alpha Sebastian only lowered his voice.","\"You know how exposed we are right now. The whole pack is watching.\"","She understood what he meant. The photos and evidence surrounding the affair could still damage them, even if they were not enough to prove every detail in court.","Serena did not dare push him further.","She gritted her teeth and walked toward the exit one painful step at a time.","Isabella watched her with a satisfied smile.","\"You know what, Mom? I actually liked Eira better as our pack’s Luna.\"","Serena’s face went cold.","Luna Margaret’s expression tightened too.","\"That’s enough.\"","--","At the hospital, Isabella was examined and sent to the waiting area with barely a scratch. Serena was still being treated. She had bruises across her body from hitting the pavement, and a nurse was applying ointment to the worst ones.","Alpha Sebastian came out first and found Isabella sitting there without a care in the world.","\"After all these years, you still can’t keep your hands or your mouth under control?\"","\"Not when someone deserves it.\" Isabella shot to her feet. \"She’s a homewrecker who drained you dry.\"","\"Isabella.\" Alpha Sebastian’s expression hardened. \"Stop calling her that. The money wasn’t all her fault. I’m the one who signed the checks.\"","Luna Margaret, who had followed him out, snapped. Her voice shook with anger and heartbreak. \"What were you thinking? Giving her some money is one thing, but handing over everything?\"","She wiped at the corner of her eye.","\"Do you know how the rest of us have lived these past few years? The Hale family should have been living comfortably. Instead, we watched every expense while Serena spent your money like it was nothing.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s chest tightened at the mention of Eira.","She resents me too.","Isabella was not interested in his guilt.","\"Then make Serena pay it back.\"","\"The money is my responsibility,\" Alpha Sebastian said coldly. \"Whether I recover it is none of your business.\"","\"Then it’s Eira’s business.\" Isabella turned toward the exit. \"There’s no way she’ll sit back and watch her husband give his entire fortune to a homewrecker.\"","\"Don’t call her that.\" Alpha Sebastian’s voice dropped. \"And stay away from Eira.\"","Isabella stopped and looked back at him.","\"Homewrecker. Homewrecker. Home...\"","His hand shot out. The slap cracked across her cheek, loud and sharp.","Isabella stumbled back and stared at him in disbelief.","\"You hit me?\" Her voice shook. \"You hit your own sister for her?\"","\"Do you even know what Serena has done for you?\" Alpha Sebastian demanded. \"Why are you acting like Serena is the only one at fault?\"","Isabella’s eyes flashed.","\"You want to know what Serena has done?\" she shouted. \"She helped set Eira up!\"","Alpha Sebastian went still.","Isabella pressed a hand to her burning cheek.","\"When Eira was drugged and almost assaulted, Serena was involved. Serena got the drug. And Serena was the one who found the man.\"","The hallway fell silent.","For the first time, Alpha Sebastian’s anger disappeared.","\"What did you just say?\""]},{"number":155,"title":"Chapter 155 The Real Puppet Master","paragraphs":["Isabella’s words hit two people at once. Her mother, and her brother.","For a second the whole hallway went quiet. The carts, the nurses, the buzzing lights, all of it dropped away. There was just his sister’s voice going around in his head.","Serena helped set Eira up. Serena picked the drug. Serena found the guy.","\"Say that again,\" Alpha Sebastian said. It came out as almost nothing.","He remembered that night. The cold water. Eira white as the sheets, soaked through, so weak she could barely stand.","Luna Margaret grabbed her daughter’s arm. \"Why are we only hearing this now? If you’d told us Serena was behind it, your father never would’ve gone after some stranger. You wouldn’t have spent all that time locked up.\"","\"Because she used me.\" Isabella’s regret was real, just too late. \" She was always buying me stuff, taking me shopping. Eira never bought me a thing. So yeah, I figured Serena was the one. If I’d known every dollar came straight out of Sebastian’s own account, I never would’ve gone along with it.\"","She turned to her brother.","\"I’m not lying this time. Setting Eira up so you’d catch her and file, that part was me. I’ll own it. But the pills, the drink, the man? That was all Serena. She walked me through every step. She even told me not to suddenly start being nice to Eira, because the two of us never got along and Eira would see it coming.\"","Luna Margaret’s eyes lost their focus for a second.","\"I’ll tell you one thing,\" she said to Alpha Sebastian, flat. \"Your sister isn’t sharp enough to plan all that on her own. Serena played this whole family. You included.\"","\"Think about it. Since the day that woman got her hooks in you, has one single thing gone right?\"","\"The money’s gone. The project’s gone.\"","She let it sit there.","\"And now Eira’s gone too.\"","Money. His career. His mate. The three things a man builds his life on, and all three went down at once.","But it was the last one that knocked the air out of him.","Eira’s gone too.","Money he could make back. A company he could build again. But a mate bond, once it’s dissolved, stays dissolved. There’s no filing to undo it. Even the woman covering her lectures had said it flat out. Eira had to be all the way done, or she never would’ve left this quietly.","Alpha Sebastian had always known the worst thing he ever did was mate her and never touch her. She’d wanted a kid. He’d been too cold for that, too. Too cheap, even.","He never laid a hand on her. Then he almost let a stranger do it for him.","His eyes went red.","\"So use it on her,\" Isabella said. \"Hold it over Serena’s head. She doesn’t pay back every dollar, I testify. I’ll put her in a cell. She can write you a check from prison, I don’t care.\"","There wasn’t a shred of guilt in her. Just the money. Three hundred grand a month. If I could claw back even part of that... She’d finally be somebody. She could walk into a room full of her friends and dare a single one of them to whisper that her own brother didn’t love her, that’s why she never had nice things.","The thought put a smile on her face, right up until it pulled at her cheek. God, that slap had landed like a brick.","This is all on Serena. She’s the one who scrambled his head.","\"Mom, my face is killing me. Have the desk call me a car, I want somebody to look at it.\"","\"It’s a slap, Isabella. You’ll live.\" Luna Margaret didn’t even glance over.","Isabella dropped onto a row of waiting-room chairs with a huff, hand pressed to her cheek, making sure every nurse who walked past caught how wronged she was.","She’d been cleared ten minutes ago. Serena was the one still back there getting stitched up. Isabella could’ve gotten up and gone home anytime she wanted. She just wasn’t going to. Not after that slap.","Let him make it up to me. He owes me.","Alpha Sebastian barely heard any of it. He’d sunk onto a chair at the end of the row, phone loose in his hand, eyes on the floor. It buzzed. He didn’t look.","Luna Margaret sat down and gently worked the phone out of his fingers.","\"Give me that. You’re in no shape to talk to anybody.\" Her voice went soft, which for her was rare. \"I’ll handle the calls. Just sit a minute.\"","He was too hollowed out to argue. He gave her the passcode without looking up and let his head fall back against the wall.","That was all she needed.","\"Come on.\" She pulled Isabella up by the arm. \"Let’s go find a nurse and get more ice on that cheek before it swells.\"","Isabella brightened and went along, finally getting the fuss she’d been fishing for. Luna Margaret walked her a little way down the hall, over toward the nurses’ station, until they were well out of Alpha Sebastian’s line of sight.","The ice was never the point.","Luna Margaret opened his banking app and went straight to the transfers.","Line after line. Wire to Serena Winthrop.","First of every month, going back years. Same name, same day, all under real names, all dated. The kind of record a court could read straight off the page.","Her jaw set. She hit record on the screen and let it run, catching every line, even the small ones tucked between the big transfers."]},{"number":156,"title":"Chapter 156 What He Couldn’t Let Go Of","paragraphs":["Luna Margaret and Isabella were gone.","Alpha Sebastian hadn’t moved. Head in his hands, then his fingers laced behind his neck, then back again, like there was no way to sit that made the last ten minutes hurt any less.","Serena spotted him from down the hall and got it completely wrong. She figured his mom and sister had been on him again about the money. She softened her steps and her eyes and came over.","\"Sebastian, honey. What happened? Was it your mom and Isabella again? I’m so sorry, I—\"","He lifted his head.","His eyes were red and raw, like an animal about to snap its chain.","The words dried up in her throat.","He just looked at her. Like he was trying to see straight through to whatever was underneath.","Serena had no idea what she’d walked into, so she kept talking to fill the quiet.","\"I just got out. They ran a urine test, my back’s still bugging me, results come back tomorrow, but honestly I feel a lot better, so you really don’t have to—\"","\"Serena.\"","She couldn’t remember the last time he’d called her that, and everything in her went tight.","\"Isabella just told me an interesting story.\" He held the anger on a short leash, giving her the same chance to explain that he’d once wanted to give Eira. \"You want to tell me your side?\"","The prescription slip started shaking in her hand.","\"What story?\" It came out as a whisper.","\"The night Eira was drugged and almost assaulted. Were you in on it? Did you get Isabella the pills? Did you find the man?\" He stood up, and now he had a good foot on her, his voice coming down cold. \"Yes or no.\"","This was the leash Isabella had held on her the whole time.","Serena just never thought the girl would yank it this fast. Over money, of all things. Money they could have worked out. And she’d blown the whole thing up in one afternoon.","Serena bit down hard on the tip of her tongue. The pain flooded her eyes, and she let it show.","\"I didn’t—\"","\"No?\" He stepped closer. \"Then chew on this. You know why I was so sure Eira was gunning for Isabella that night? Because everybody knows that girl isn’t sharp enough to pull something like this off on her own.\"","Eira had warned him. She’d hinted at it, right in front of Serena.","And he’d waved it off.","Four years. Four years he’d never once dragged his feet for Eira.","He’d just been angry that night. Too busy being angry to ever get around to being scared. Because every single time, Serena had been right there at his side, soft as could be, feeding the fire.","\"So was it you?\" It came out as a roar, the veins standing out in his neck.","Serena had seen him this angry only once before.","The last time was when she slipped out of California without a word, and he finally tracked her down.","That time it was about her.","This time it was about Eira.","\"Sebastian. You’d really yell at me like this over her?\"","\"Don’t change the subject.\"","He watched the tears well up, the lip start to tremble, the whole wounded-bird act. And for the first time he saw it for what it was. A performance.","Her tears spilled over. \"You already think it was me. So why bother asking?\"","\"Do not change the subject.\" He bit off every word. His patience was gone. \"Yes or no. That’s all I want.\"","\"Can we take this outside?\" She wiped her cheek. \"People come through here all the time, and with who you are, if the wrong person snaps a photo—\"","\"Let them.\" He knocked her hand off his arm. \"I asked you to explain and you won’t. I asked you yes or no and you won’t. You want me to dig it up myself? Or do you figure I can’t?\"","He leaned in.","\"And if I can’t, you think the cops will have the same problem?\"","Serena did the math in a heartbeat.","Cops. If he was only threatening to call them, that meant coming clean might keep them out of it.","She couldn’t afford another black mark.","Her grandfather was already sidelined, no project of his own to hide her under for years.","Any lab worth joining ran a full background check, and Vincent had bailed her out once already. There wouldn’t be a second time. One more incident and it stuck to her for good.","She set her jaw.","\"Fine. Yes. It was me.\" Then, fast: \"But not just me, Sebastian. Isabella too. The whole thing was her idea.\"","Chaining herself to the girl. Betting he’d never throw them both under the bus over one Eira.","He heard it for exactly what it was. She’d confessed and threatened him in the same breath.","Cute.","His mouth twitched. \"It really was you. Why? Why would you do that?\"","\"You honestly don’t know?\" She looked him dead in the eye. \"I love you. You can’t see that? I never said it out loud? I didn’t want to lose you. I wanted to marry you. That’s all.\"","\"You’d give me anything. Everything. Everything except your name. Was I supposed to be the other woman forever?\"","\"You know who I am, Sebastian? I’m a Winthrop. From a powerful pack. And I threw all of it away to be your dirty little secret.\"","Her face crumpled.","\"I love you. I don’t care what anybody says.\"","\"Then why her?\" he said. \"You’ll walk away from anything, but not Eira. Why is it always Eira you can’t let go of?\"","She’d been dying to ask it for months. She asked it now.","\"Are you in love with her?\"","\"Yes. I love her.\"","It was out before he could stop it.","The one thing he’d refused to look at, refused to name. Serena had backed him into a corner and pulled the answer right out of him.","The whole hall went dead quiet.","Serena kept crying, no sound to it now."]},{"number":157,"title":"Chapter 157 The Two of Us","paragraphs":["Serena laughed, and there was nothing warm in it. \"You love Eira. Great. So where the hell does that leave me?\"","\"Four years married to that woman and you never so much as gave her a pup. Four years, and you saved yourself for me.\"","\"And now it’s, what, we were just friends?\" She slapped a hand against her chest. \"Friends don’t do what we did after that party. Both of us wasted, and we ended up in bed. Friends don’t kiss the way you kissed me at that gala. So don’t stand there and feed me that ’friend’ line.\"","Alpha Sebastian had nothing.","\"You’re up in my face about Eira. You ever once ask yourself why I did it? You gave me everything, Sebastian. My body, your money, all those big promises. Everything but your last name. So what was I supposed to do, huh? Sit in the dark and be your little secret till I died?\"","All that ’I don’t care where we stand, I’m fine in the shadows’ talk. It had never been anything but her running out the clock.","Serena pulled in a breath and lifted her chin, scraping together whatever pride she had left.","\"I didn’t do this to Eira. You did. This one’s on you.\"","Every word hit like a fist.","Alpha Sebastian rocked back on his heels.","She kept going, driving it in. \"Am I wrong? We’re both dirty here. You want somebody to blame, start with the guy in the mirror.\"","Crack.","His own hand came up and he backhanded himself across the face.","Because she wasn’t wrong. He was garbage. Simple as that.","Serena froze. He’d hit himself. Over Eira. He was really that far gone on her?","\"Alright. Since we’re saying it all out loud.\" His voice snagged, then dropped into something flat and done. \"We’re over, Serena.\"","\"I loved you once. I’ll cop to that. But that ship’s sailed.\"","\"You’re really dumping me?\" Tears spilled down her cheeks. \"Just like that? We’re over?\"","\"Yeah. We’re over.\" Alpha Sebastian nodded. \"I’m letting the past go. I’ve got a life to get back to.\"","\"Eira.\" Her eyes reddened. \"You’re going back to her, aren’t you? She’s the life you want now.\"","He nodded.","\"You actually think she still wants you?\" Serena let out a wet little laugh. \"She’s been ghosting you for weeks. You can’t see that, or you just won’t?\"","Walking away wasn’t going to be as clean as he’d hoped.","\"I screwed her over. She’s got every right to be pissed.\"","\"Aren’t you scared she asks you for a divorce?\"","Scared. His hand shook. He was scared out of his mind.","But she hadn’t asked. Not yet. Clean up this mess with Serena and there was still a road back. Keep dragging Serena around and he’d lose Eira for real.","Four years. He’d gotten used to having her there.","Hell, he wanted a pup with her now. That old, ugly plan to trap her with a baby, back then he was too dumb to see it for what it was. That was just his heart talking, and he hadn’t been listening.","This past month without her, he’d been off. Like somebody reached in and scooped something out of his chest and left a cold hole where it used to sit. He’d drowned it in work and told himself he was fine. That’s the only reason it took him this long to figure it out.","He was done getting this wrong.","Alpha Sebastian’s mouth went tight. \"This ends here, Serena. I’m not making the same mistake twice.\"","\"And how do you figure you’re gonna end it?\" Serena fired back. \"My career’s hanging by a thread, and you’re out. Your parents and your sister are all coming after me, and you’re out. Eira decides to press charges, and you’re out then too.\"","\"Where’s your spine, Sebastian? You want to do right by Eira. Fine. Who does right by me?\"","\"The money, I’ve got,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"I’ll get my parents to back off. They’ll drop it. And Eira’s on me. I’ll handle her myself.\"","Money was the exact thing Serena was sweating.","Without Alpha Sebastian, who was going to cover her research? Nobody else opened their wallet the way he did.","She wasn’t about to let him cut her loose that easy. But standing here running in circles in a hospital hallway wasn’t getting her anywhere.","\"Your sister worked me over pretty good today, in case you forgot. She’s your sister. Least you can do is take care of the woman she put in the ER. I want to go home and lie down.\"","Alpha Sebastian frowned. She wasn’t wrong. But getting spotted with Serena again was one more thing he’d never be able to explain to Eira.","\"I’ll have Beta Jordan run you home.\"","\"Sebastian!\" Her chest was heaving now. \"You won’t even drive me home yourself?\"","He’d said he was keeping his distance, and he meant it. He didn’t take her anywhere. He called Beta Jordan instead.","\"Get Miss Winthrop home. Make sure she gets in okay.\"","It wasn’t long before Beta Jordan arrived.","He clocked the red handprint blooming across his boss’s cheek, then his gaze swept over the cold, buttoned-up Miss Winthrop.","It didn’t take him two seconds to piece it together.","They were done.","Blowup or clean break, either way, staying on Serena’s good side couldn’t hurt.","\"Miss Winthrop. Right this way.\"","Serena didn’t move an inch.","Alpha Sebastian was already gone, off to find his mother and his sister."]},{"number":158,"title":"Chapter 158 The Grapevine","paragraphs":["Number Nine, Southridge Estates.","Lila was mid-story, selling it to Mrs. Jones like she’d just had the best afternoon of her life.","\"You should’ve seen what Isabella did to Serena. Ten bucks says she’s black and blue under that outfit. Solid work too, her aim just needed a little tuning. Two inches to the left and Serena’s picking teeth up off the floor.\" She looked genuinely bummed about the teeth.","Eira’s disappointment ran the other way. \"I just want to know how it went down once Sebastian showed up.\"","\"Relax, I’m on it.\" Lila’s grin turned wicked. She waved her phone. \"I had Sebastian’s whole circus followed. My guy’s been texting me updates all afternoon, and he’s about to swing by with the rest.\"","The doorbell rang right on cue.","Mrs. Jones had it open before the second ring. Alpha Killian’s driver stood on the step.","Lila lit up like it was her birthday. \"Okay, sit, sit. What happened? And please tell me you got video.\"","\"Alpha Sebastian hauled all three of them to the ER first,\" the driver said. \"Then it kicked off again. Except this round it wasn’t Isabella and Serena. It was Sebastian and Serena.\"","Lila’s jaw dropped. \"Get out.\"","Eira turned, thrown too. \"Sebastian and Serena? Not Sebastian and Isabella?\"","\"Nope.\" The driver held up his phone. \"They went at it right there in the hallway. Not screaming, but not exactly keeping it down either. I grabbed a stretch that sounded like it mattered. Figured you’d want it, Miss Crawford. Already AirDropped a copy to myself so it’s backed up.\"","\"Thank you.\" Eira took the phone. \"Did either of them say anything that actually lands as cheating?\"","\"Not in so many words,\" he admitted. \"But Alpha Killian always says enough small stuff adds up. Sooner or later one piece does the job.\"","Eira looked up, caught off guard. \"Killian told you to record this?\"","The driver nodded. \"A while back. Anything with Sebastian or Serena in it, if I can get it on camera, get it. Said one of these days a clip would come in handy for you.\"","Something in Lila’s chest went soft. \"God. My brother is so gone on you it’s honestly a little sad to watch.\"","\"Alpha Killian double-checks anything that touches Miss Crawford. More than he does his own deals.\" Mrs. Jones set a bowl of chips and salsa on the coffee table and settled into the armchair.","Eira sighed. \"Mrs. Jones.\"","Mrs. Jones raised a hand, solemn. \"I swear this one isn’t a line out of a book. If it were, I’d have gone with something like, it’s the first time in his life the man’s ever put a woman ahead of himself.\"","There it was.","Eira bit back a laugh, grabbed a soda off the table, and slid it across to her. \"Drink your Coke, Mrs. Jones.\"","Lila’s hand shot out. \"Hey. Where’s mine?\"","\"Baby,\" Eira said, but she cracked open another can and slid it over anyway.","Eira’s smile widened, enough that her teeth showed.","Mrs. Jones gasped. \"She smiled. She actually smiled.\"","Eira put a hand over her face.","\"Mrs. Jones, how many of those romance audiobooks have you got going, seriously?\" Lila asked.","\"I just leave them running while I work.\" Her eyes crinkled into happy slits. \"And it landed, didn’t it? Got the girl to smile.\"","Eira waved them both off and pulled up the video.","Lila leaned in close to the speaker. \"She keeps saying something about being wasted, some party, saving herself? The hell’s that supposed to mean?\"","Eira knew exactly what it meant.","\"Sebastian and Serena slept together. Drunk, after some party.\"","\"They slept together?\" Lila shot upright. \"That’s a smoking gun. Whatever hotel it was, we pull the booking, grab the security cams—\"","\"It wasn’t a hotel.\" Eira shook her head. \"It was at the house.\"","Lila’s fists curled. \"Isabella went way too easy today. Should’ve saved a couple swings for her own brother.\"","Mrs. Jones’s eyes went glassy, but she kept it together and said nothing.","\"It’s over now.\" Eira said it light, like it was nothing. She left out the part where she’d thrown up for hours that day, dry-heaving till there was nothing left but bile.","On screen, the two of them finally split off and walked opposite directions.","Lila frowned. \"Why’d they split up? Sebastian’s actually giving up on his precious first love?\"","\"He’s not.\" Four years, and Sebastian had never so much as looked at anyone but Serena. A man like that didn’t just flip a switch overnight. Eira wasn’t buying it. She had the driver AirDrop her the file.","\"Sebastian drove back to Southridge too,\" the driver added.","Mrs. Jones snorted. \"So that’s why my phone won’t quit. Speak of the devil.\"","Lila blinked. \"Devil?\"","\"Sebastian,\" Eira said.","\"Sure enough, he went straight to Number Twenty and he’s been leaning on the doorbell ever since.\" Mrs. Jones pulled up the door cam. There he was, same clothes as the video.","\"Eira? You in there? I know you’re home. Open up. Five minutes, that’s all. Just look at me.\"","His voice crackled through the speaker. Eira’s brow had barely started to knit before Mrs. Jones, quick as anything, cut the feed.","They figured killing the door cam would shut it down.","Nope. Alpha Sebastian had made up his mind. Until Eira opened that door and looked him in the eye, he wasn’t going anywhere. He just kept leaning on the bell and calling her name, dead set on being a pain in the ass to the bitter end.","The houses in Southridge sat far apart, walled off by enough landscaping to eat any noise, so he wasn’t bugging the neighbors.","But the estate ran patrols, and a quiet property was the whole point.","Every time a guard rolled past, Alpha Sebastian went still as a lawn statue. The second they left, he started right back up.","Word got to Alpha Killian on his way in. He told the driver to swing by Number Twenty.","In the dark, under a streetlamp, Alpha Sebastian was still out there.","\"Guy’s been at it since four,\" the driver said. \"Three hours, easy.\"","Alpha Killian’s eyes went flat. \"Tell the guards to let him stand there. The longer, the better. They don’t have to touch him.\"","The driver nodded and the car rolled on toward Number Nine.","The headlights hadn’t even died before Mrs. Jones came out the front door, all smiles. \"Alpha Killian! Wasn’t expecting you.\"","The driver gave an innocent shrug. \"Wrong turn, Alpha. Long as we’re here, though, you might as well grab dinner. I’ll have Mrs. Jones see if Miss Crawford’s up for company.\"","Alpha Killian still didn’t say a word.","But he got out of the car.","Mrs. Jones ducked back inside. \"Miss Crawford, the driver made a wrong turn and dropped Alpha Killian here. Want me to set him a place, or send him back to Number One?\"","The man was already on the doorstep. You didn’t send a guest packing, and Eira had manners. So she went out herself. \"Killian. Come on in.\"","He climbed out and gave the driver a flat look.","The driver just grinned. \"I’ll be at Number One. Text me when you need a ride.\""]},{"number":159,"title":"Chapter 159 The Nose That Followed","paragraphs":["Alpha Killian started up the walk. Lila appeared in the doorway, shoulder against the frame, and sing-songed, \"Killiaan, come on iiin—\"","His eyes cut to her. \"Stand up straight.\"","\"Cut the act.\" Lila rolled her eyes.","They sat down. Mrs. Jones ran through the whole menu dish by dish, and it clicked for Eira what she was really up to. Selling her. Every plate was another line in the pitch. See how she cooks? See how she’s settling in? You’d be crazy to let this one go.","\"One dish tonight’s extra special, Killian.\"Lila carried it out like a trophy. \"Loaded mac and cheese. Eira made it from scratch. Lucky you.\"","Alpha Killian raised a brow. \"Hm.\" The end of it tipped up, just barely.","\"It’s mac and cheese.\" Eira thought they were both ridiculous. \"It’s not fancy.\"","\"Nothing she makes is basic.\" Lila held it out of reach, chin up. \"And she made it for me. I said I was craving it. You’re eating it because of me, so get that straight.\"","Alpha Killian let out a low laugh, and on his first move at the table dragged two-thirds of it onto his own plate.","Lila gaped. \"You have got to be kidding me.\"","He ate slow and neat, looking like he enjoyed her outrage more than the food. When she lunged for the dish, he pinned the serving spoon flat on top of it. \"Grab it and you’ll wear it.\"","\"Then let go—Eira, do something!\"","Alpha Killian looked at her too, and his eyes said, handle the one on your right.","Eira sat wedged between them and made the only sane call. She got up to make a second batch.","She’d barely reached for a pot when the light shifted behind her.","A shadow fell across the counter, and then he was there, close enough that she felt the warmth of him before she heard a word.","Warm fingers lifted the spoon out of her hand and set it down.","\"Go eat.\" His voice came low, right against her ear.","Eira didn’t turn around. She stared at the cutting board, suddenly aware of her own pulse. \"I’m not fighting your sister over mac and cheese.\"","His hand came to rest on her shoulder and turned her around to face him. He was closer than she’d expected, close enough that she had to tilt her chin. The kitchen felt smaller all at once, the noise from the next room fading to nothing.","He brushed a strand of hair off her cheek, his palm curving briefly around the back of her neck, unhurried, like he had every right to be there. Then he reached past her waist for the apron strings.","Eira went still.","He didn’t look down. He kept his eyes on hers, watching the color climb into her face while his hands worked the knot loose at the small of her back, one slow pull and then the next. His knuckles grazed her spine through the fabric, and she felt it all the way up.","The apron came free between them. Neither of them moved for a second longer than they should have.","\"Where’s it go?\" he asked, quiet.","It took her a moment to find her voice. She pointed to the hook on the wall.","He hung it up, and the space between them opened back up, the ordinary sounds of the house rushing in to fill it. He tipped his head toward the table.","She followed him out on legs that felt a half-second behind.","Lila was watching them come back with a slow, knowing smile. \"You know what? I’m out. He can have the whole pan.\"","She propped her chin in her hand. \"Poor guy only gets to eat with Eira once in a blue moon.\"","Alpha Killian understood, with grim clarity, that the single biggest obstacle on his long road forward was his own sister.","--","Meanwhile, Alpha Sebastian had been camped outside Number Twenty for going on four hours.","Lights on inside. But no matter how he leaned on the bell or what he called out, nothing moved. The place felt hollow.","Once the doubt set in, he quit the doorstep and started circling the house.","Dragging a hand along a shut window frame, he felt it. A thick coat of dust. Everywhere else was spotless. This one corner wasn’t.","That wasn’t Eira. She had a mild obsessive streak about cleaning and never missed a corner. And if a housekeeper worked the place, they’d have come down by now and run him off. Nobody had.","He stepped back and looked again. No warmth, no life. Nobody lived here.","Either Jordan had it wrong, or Jordan had been fed a lie and this whole house was bait. And he didn’t have to guess who’d set it.","The day he came to lease, Alpha Killian had shown up in person, a housekeeper trailing him.","The whole development was Sterling-built, and Alpha Killian lived in the crown jewel, the only address marked with a capital One.","Worth a shot.","He’d never clear the gate at Number One, so he pulled up to the guard booth. \"Looking for the housekeeper who runs Number One. She left something at my unit last time I leased.\"","\"Mrs. Jones?\" One guard glanced at the other. \"She’s not at Number One much these days. Usually over at Number Nine.\"","Alpha Sebastian drove straight for Number Nine.","Immaculate yard. Every window lit. He rolled his window down, and through the glass caught a silhouette that stopped him cold.","It looked exactly like Eira.","He was out of the car before he’d thought it through. The iron gate had a walk-through door set into it, standing open, and he let himself in. The closer he got, the clearer the sounds through a white door left ajar. Voices. Laughing.","\"Mrs. Jones, when’d the cherries show up?\" Lila plucked a dark one off the stem and dropped it on Eira’s plate. \"Try it. Stupid good.\"","\"Came this afternoon.\" Mrs. Jones set down a bowl. \"There’s more where that came from, so don’t be shy.\"","Eira turned the cherry over between her fingers before she ate it. She’d priced fruit like this once, in a display case at some upscale market she’d only ever walked past. She hadn’t bought it. She’d put it back and picked up the bag on sale.","Here it just showed up in a bowl, and nobody at the table so much as blinked.","Old habits. She caught herself doing the math on a single piece of fruit and made herself stop.","Juice slid to the corner of her mouth before she noticed.","Alpha Killian’s hand was there before it could drip. He caught it with a napkin and wiped her lip, calm, like it was nothing.","Eira went still.","\"You’re a hundred miles away,\" he said, low, close enough that only she caught it. His thumb rested a beat at the edge of her jaw. \"It’s just cherries. Eat.\"","She blinked up at him, and only then did it land, how close he was, that it was his hand at her chin.","That was the exact second Alpha Sebastian reached the window.","Something in him snapped. His eyes went red and he slammed his knuckles against the glass.","Every head at the table turned.","Eira saw him and frowned.","Alpha Sebastian hit the white door, found it unlatched, and shoved through. He crossed to Eira, hand already reaching to haul her up. \"What the hell is this?\"","Alpha Killian’s arm went around Eira’s waist in the same breath his boot drove into Alpha Sebastian’s gut. One clean motion.","Alpha Sebastian staggered back two steps, eyes wide with disbelief."]},{"number":160,"title":"Chapter 160 No Claws Toward People","paragraphs":["Watching Alpha Sebastian stagger from the kick, Lila and Mrs. Jones quietly raised their hands and gave two slow, soft claps.","Nice. Well kicked.","Eira’s first instinct wasn’t to look at Alpha Sebastian. It was to look at the man beside her.","Alpha Killian’s eyes held something Eira had never seen in them. Pure, cold contempt. The look you’d give roadkill on the shoulder of the highway.","His voice matched it, low and edged. \"Alpha Sebastian. An animal doesn’t get to put its paws on a person. Count yourself lucky a boot’s all you got.\"","Alpha Sebastian caught his balance. Even through the sting, his eyes went to Eira.","She wasn’t looking at him. She hadn’t looked at him once. Her whole attention was fixed on the man beside her, quiet and steady, the way she used to look at him years ago, before he taught her not to bother.","The jealousy came up his throat fast. He forced it back down. He’d come to make peace, not to detonate.","He pulled in a breath and gentled his voice. \"Eira. Come here. Come to me.\"","The hand at her waist tightened. No warning, just a sudden, deliberate pressure, fingers spreading against her side, holding her in place. Like Alpha Killian genuinely thought she might get up and cross the room to him.","Eira felt it before she understood it. The warmth of his palm through her clothes, the quiet certainty in the way he held on, like the answer had already been decided and he was simply making sure of it.","She glanced down at the hand splayed over her side. Her pulse did something strange.","The first time he’d held her here, it was so Alpha Sebastian couldn’t drag her off. That she understood. That was protection.","But Alpha Sebastian wasn’t touching her now. Nobody was dragging her anywhere. So what was this hand for?","She didn’t dare look up at him.","She was suddenly, uncomfortably sure that if she did, she’d find him already watching her, already knowing exactly what that little catch in her breath meant.","So she kept her eyes on Alpha Sebastian instead, and made her voice flat and final. \"Sebastian. Get out.\"","The second the words left her, the hand at her waist eased.","And that, somehow, unsettled her more than the holding had.","Alpha Killian turned to Mrs. Jones. \"Call security. Have him removed.\"","\"On it.\" But Mrs. Jones was already muttering as she went. \"Security. By the time they show he’ll have taken root. I’ll handle it myself.\"","She came back with the broom from the mudroom and planted herself in front of Alpha Sebastian like a bouncer, blocking Alpha Killian and Eira behind her so he couldn’t even see the couch anymore.","\"Here’s how this goes, Alpha Sebastian.\" She leveled the broom at his chest. \"You get one polite ask, then it stops being polite. So. Walking out on your own, or you want to see what this thing can do?\"","Lila called over from the table. \"Just run him off, Mrs. Jones. Anything you tear, I’ll replace. Anything you bruise, I’ll cover the ER.\"","\"You got it.\" Mrs. Jones jabbed the broom into his chest and started walking him backward. \"Out. Come on. Out. Quit hounding Miss Crawford.\"","Alpha Sebastian, who lived and died by a clean shirt, batted at the bristles with a grimace, eyes still locked on Eira.","\"Eira. You’re really going to stand there and let the Sterlings treat me like this?\"","\"You stood there and let the Hales treat me like this for four years.\" She got to her feet and started toward him.","He’d already been herded to the doorway. His heel found empty air, and though he didn’t fall, he was forced down off the threshold and out into the yard.","Eira came to the door and stood above him, high enough that he had to tilt his head up to see her.","\"Eira, I know you’re mad about how my family treated you. I already tore into Isabella. And I changed the code on our place. Nobody walks in and out whenever they feel like it anymore.\"","Mrs. Jones leaned an elbow on the broom and scoffed. \"Where was all that Alpha swagger before? Little late. Nobody’s buying.\"","\"Wouldn’t feed that line to a dog,\" Lila said.","Alpha Sebastian acted like he didn’t hear them, eyes locked on Eira, pleading now. \"Eira, let me get you a better place. We’ll buy somewhere better. Better than whatever rental Alpha Killian set you up in.\"","\"You’ve got a filthy mind, Alpha Sebastian.\" Alpha Killian stepped out beside Eira, his shadow falling across her as he moved half a step in front of her.","\"You buy women houses, so you figure every house a woman lives in must have been bought by some man.\" He let out a low, cold laugh.","Alpha Sebastian froze.","Eira picked it up, voice cool. \"Sorry to disappoint. This house is mine.\"","\"I’m sorry, Eira. I misread it.\" He scrambled to walk it back.","\"You’ve misread me more times than I can count. You want to walk out on your own, or should Mrs. Jones walk you out with the broom?\"","Something ached in Alpha Sebastian’s chest. He dropped his voice and his pride with it. \"I know I got you wrong. I’ve said I’m sorry. Can’t you come home? I need you.\"","\"You mean you need an unpaid live-in maid.\" Anger flared in Eira.","\"Sebastian. If you’d spent even a fraction of that money on staff, you could’ve had ten housekeepers and lived like a king. You weren’t running things that lean because you had to. You just liked squeezing every last bit of work out of me.\"","\"I swear, from now on, you control every penny.\" He meant it.","\"And what would I want with your finances?\" She almost laughed.","\"Finances?\" Lila ran a chilly look up and down him. \"Big talk for a guy running on pocket change. Serena already bled you dry, didn’t she?\" Her eyes traveled the length of him on the last word, plainly suggesting he’d been drained in more ways than one.","His neck went red.","\"If Alpha Sebastian actually feels bad about how he treated Eira,\" Lila went on, \"he’ll make Serena pay back every dime he spent on her.\"","Eira watched him, waiting for that answer too.","His lips parted. Nothing came out.","He’d just drawn his line with Serena, and the price of that clean break had been writing off every cent he’d ever spent on her.","His brow furrowed.","Eira had known he couldn’t answer. Or wouldn’t.","\"Sebastian.\" She said his name.","His head came up at once, a faint light in his eyes, sure he was about to hear her let it all go.","Wishful thinking.","\"You don’t even have to say a word to Serena,\" Eira said. \"All you have to do is admit you two were lovers. That makes every dollar you spent on her money spent during our marriage. It’s a shared marital debt.\"","His eyes widened a fraction. She was genuinely working out how to claw that money back.","His fingers trembled at his side.","\"Guess the apology wasn’t sincere after all.\" Alpha Killian glanced at Mrs. Jones.","\"On it!\" Mrs. Jones hoisted the broom and charged, driving it at his chest. \"Out. Now. Move. And don’t come back. You show up here again, you get this again.\"","\"The nerve. Cheats, keeps a mistress, and still struts around with his chin up. Lied to Miss Crawford for four years and that’s not enough, he wants to keep lying. Animal.\"","Alpha Sebastian backed toward the door under the assault, trying to get a word of explanation out, only for the broom to catch him full across the face.","\"Ugh.\" Lila grimaced.","A small laugh slipped out of Eira before she could stop it.","Alpha Sebastian caught it. That laugh.","Worse than the broom in his face was the sight of Eira smiling because he’d been humiliated.","Did she really just... not care at all anymore?"]},{"number":161,"title":"Chapter 161 The Report","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian left Number Nine like a stray turned out into the rain, silent and hollow.","Back at the Hale apartment, he scrubbed his face raw. Then he brushed his teeth until half a tube of toothpaste was gone, as if he could scrub the entire afternoon out of his mouth.","Serena called while he was squeezing out the last drop.","He saw her name, frowned, and answered. \"What?\"","His voice was cold and flat. He had already made up his mind. Serena was out of his life. He would win Eira back and build a life with her.","Serena dropped her sweet voice at once. \"The clinic called. Something was wrong with my lab work. They want me back tomorrow at ten. Isabella put me in the ER. As her brother, shouldn’t you handle that?\"","The request caught him off guard. \"Ten. Fine.\"","He started to hang up.","\"Sebastian, you’re really going to treat me like this? After all these years, am I worth less to you than Eira?\"","He closed his eyes and took a slow breath. \"Serena, we ended a long time ago. When you left for Europe. When I married Eira. That should have been the end of it.\"","\"But it wasn’t. We were happy together.\"","\"If we were happy, we wouldn’t be here.\" He walked into the bedroom and stared at Eira’s new clothes hanging in the closet. The room still felt empty without her. \"She’s coming after our shared assets. I’ve done what I can to protect us. But if you keep this up and someone finds proof, I can’t help you.\"","\"Can’t help me?\" Serena’s voice rose. \"That money was yours to give. What about all your promises? Eira comes back, and suddenly I’m disposable?\"","Alpha Sebastian hung up.","Then he looked around the bedroom.","Something was missing.","Eira’s small belongings had once filled the room. Keepsakes on the shelves. Hair ties on the nightstand. Little things that made the penthouse feel lived in.","Now everything was gone.","He opened the closet. Her old clothes had disappeared. He searched the guest room and opened every storage box.","Not one shirt remained.","His heartbeat turned uneven.","He called Jordan. \"Did you throw out Eira’s clothes?\"","\"No. Nobody touched her things, Alpha Sebastian. I thought you cleared them out yourself. You wanted to buy her a new wardrobe.\"","\"I didn’t clear anything.\" Alpha Sebastian’s chest tightened. \"When does someone take every last thing they own out of a home?\"","Jordan knew the answer. He also knew better than to say it.","\"When they hate the place, I guess.\"","Alpha Sebastian seized on that excuse. He had brought Serena back to the Hale apartment. Eira hated Serena, so she must hate the home too.","That had to be it.","\"Find me a moving company,\" he ordered. \"I’m moving to Number Eleven in Southridge tomorrow.\"","It was only a few houses from Number Nine, close enough to walk.","Number Twenty had been Alpha Killian’s trap.","This time, Alpha Sebastian thought, he had made the smart move.","--","Southridge, Number Nine","\"I want to move as soon as I can,\" Eira said.","Mrs. Jones’s eyes lit up. \"How about tomorrow, Miss Crawford?\"","\"Tomorrow?\" Eira glanced down at her untouched drink. \"I only just got the keys. I haven’t even seen the place yet.\"","Alpha Killian’s gaze shifted to her. \"Where is it?\"","\"10 Ashford Lane.\"","Lila’s eyebrows shot up. She turned to Alpha Killian with a slow, knowing look. Was he about to buy a place there just so he could live closer to Eira?","Not that he needed another property. Alpha Killian owned real estate all over the country.","\"10 Ashford Lane?\" Lila repeated. \"Wait, where is that?\"","\"Ashford Lane,\" Alpha Killian said. Something thoughtful flickered in his eyes. \"You can’t just show up there. The residents’ association requires registration, paperwork, and a background check. You won’t get inside tonight.\"","He looked back at Eira. \"Give it two days before you move.\"","Eira nodded. \"Then I’ll go see it tomorrow.\"","\"Take me with you!\" Lila grabbed her arm.","\"I want to leave first thing in the morning,\" Eira said. If everything went smoothly, she could be moved in by afternoon.","Lila’s excitement faded. She was the kind of person who could sleep until noon without even trying. Her mouth pulled into a dramatic pout.","Eira laughed before she could stop herself. \"Can you be ready by nine?\"","Lila brightened at once. \"Absolutely.\"","\"Drop the wounded-puppy routine,\" Alpha Killian muttered.","\"Not my fault you never learned how to use it.\" Lila stuck out her tongue. \"Jealous much?\"","Alpha Killian stood. At the door, he glanced back at Eira. \"I’ll have two guards posted here until you move.\"","Eira started to protest, but Mrs. Jones was already nodding.","\"Good call, Alpha Killian. Then we won’t have to worry about that doorbell creep hanging around.\"","--","9:00 a.m. the next morning","Lila stumbled out of Number Nine beside Eira, yawning so hard her eyes watered.","\"I’m fine to drive,\" she insisted.","\"You can barely keep your eyes open.\" Eira opened the rideshare app, called a car, and guided her into the back seat.","They had barely left Southridge when Jordan appeared at the gate, speaking with security. A moving truck was scheduled for that afternoon, and he needed to put it on the access list.","At ten, Alpha Sebastian stood outside the clinic, waiting for Serena.","She arrived late and looked terrible. Her face was pale, her eyes were bloodshot, and dark circles showed beneath them. She had clearly spent the night crying instead of sleeping.","Alpha Sebastian glanced at her. \"Let’s go.\"","She had expected him to ask if she was okay. Instead, that was all she got.","With an annoyed huff, Serena walked ahead of him.","In the exam room, Alpha Sebastian looked at the doctor. \"What came back abnormal?\"","The doctor checked Serena’s chart. \"There was an irregularity in the urinalysis, so we’re repeating it and adding a pregnancy test.\"","Alpha Sebastian frowned. \"A pregnancy test?\"","\"We’re checking for hCG.\" The doctor looked between them. \"Are you her boyfriend or her husband?\"","\"Pregnant?\" Serena blurted.","A flash of delight crossed her face.","Alpha Sebastian went silent.","The doctor lifted a hand. \"Let’s not jump to conclusions. Serena, has your period been late?\"","She froze. She honestly had no idea. The past few weeks had been one disaster after another, and stress had thrown off her cycle before.","But if she was pregnant, everything could change.","Alpha Sebastian would never abandon his own child. The Hale Pack would not allow it either. Hope rushed through her so fast she could barely breathe.","For once, luck seemed to be on her side.","Alpha Sebastian’s expression darkened. \"How long until we get the results?\"","\"Usually thirty minutes to two hours. Leave the sample with the lab. We’ll send the results through the patient portal, and you’ll get a text when they’re ready.\"","\"Thank you, Doctor,\" Serena said, forcing herself to sound calm.","Alpha Sebastian did not say another word. His jaw stayed tight while they waited.","Fifty minutes later, Serena’s phone buzzed.","Her lab report was ready."]},{"number":162,"title":"Chapter 162 The Evidence","paragraphs":["Ashford Lane","It took Eira and Lila nearly two hours to finish the security process at 10 Ashford Lane.","The guard checked Eira’s name against the resident list, then looked over Lila’s sedan.","\"Dr. Crawford, the vehicle needs to be registered too. Only approved cars can enter. Unregistered vehicles have to stay outside the gate.\"","Eira didn’t own a car.","\"What about a moving truck?\" Lila asked. \"Can it get temporary access?\"","\"Yes, but the request must be submitted at least two hours ahead of time. We need the moving company’s name, the driver’s ID, the license plate, the make, the model, and the color. If anything doesn’t match, the truck stays outside.\"","Lila whistled. \"This place has tighter security than an airport.\"","The guard barely reacted. With his straight posture and serious expression, he looked like a former soldier.","\"So every time I visit, Eira has to come down and let me in?\" Lila asked.","\"We can always meet for lunch,\" she added quickly. \"It’s not a big deal.\"","Eira caught the disappointment in her voice and turned to the guard. \"Can I register one of her cars under my name?\"","Lila stared at her. \"You can do that?\"","\"Dr. Crawford can register one guest vehicle each month,\" the guard said. \"She’ll be responsible for it while it’s on the property. The association won’t cover any trouble the vehicle causes.\"","Eira nodded. \"Register one of your cars. Use something ordinary.\"","Lila’s eyes stung. She pressed a hand to her chest. \"I’ll pay you back by being the best little sister on the planet.\"","Eira glanced at her. \"You’re already making this sound like a business deal.\"","\"Fine. I’ll just be your favorite.\"","\"You’re my only little sister.\"","\"Exactly. I’ve got this in the bag.\"","Eira laughed.","Lila registered a sleek black sedan. Her grandparents had bought it for Luna Seraphina years earlier, and Luna Seraphina had passed it down to Lila when she turned eighteen. Once the guard entered the information, he sent the temporary access pass to Lila’s phone.","Then he waved them through.","He led them down a quiet lane shaded by tall oaks and maples. At the end stood a three-story brownstone converted into two private residences.","The building was old but well maintained. Its dark brick facade showed its age, and a short set of steps led to the entrance. Tall windows lined the upper floors, with a few window AC units sticking out from the frames. White drainpipes followed the corners, and neatly secured utility lines crossed parts of the brickwork.","Low hedges bordered the small iron fence.","Ashford Lane felt far removed from the city. No traffic, shouting, or strangers passing by. Only the rustle of leaves and the occasional car in the distance.","Eira’s unit occupied the entire third floor.","She unlocked the door, and she and Lila stepped inside.","The apartment had two bedrooms, a formal living room, a small dining room, a kitchen, and one full bathroom. The front rooms were shaded by the trees, while the south-facing windows at the back filled the apartment with light.","The layout had potential.","The rest needed work.","Dark walnut floors, faded yellow walls, heavy furniture, and old light fixtures made the place feel stuck in another decade. The sofa had lost its shape, and the dining chairs were worn around the edges.","Lila turned in a slow circle. \"The light is great, but this furniture has got to go. What’s your style?\"","\"Mid-century modern.\" Eira looked around. \"I’ll redo the whole place.\"","She took photos of every room with her phone, already planning the renovation. The walls needed fresh paint. The kitchen cabinets had to be replaced, and the bathroom needed a full update. She would send the photos and measurements to a design firm and get the work started as soon as possible.","Eira would not be moving in yet. Not with the apartment looking like this.","By noon, they finished the walkthrough and left the brownstone.","They grabbed lunch at a nearby diner. Eira had barely opened the menu when her phone rang.","Margaret Hale.","She stared at the name for a moment, then answered.","\"I found something,\" Luna Margaret said. Her voice still carried the same commanding edge. \"Come meet me.\"","Eira no longer flinched when Luna Margaret gave orders. \"If you want the money, you come to me.\"","She texted the diner’s address.","Luna Margaret gave a cold little scoff. \"Stay there.\"","Lila’s eyes lit up. \"Wow. Mention money, and suddenly she has time. Let’s hope what she found is worth the trouble.\"","\"It’s better than nothing.\" Eira needed more than proof that Alpha Sebastian and Serena had slept together. She had to prove that he had used marital money to support the affair.","Every piece counted.","Susan had warned her that they still needed stronger proof. A long history of Serena and Alpha Sebastian calling each other husband and wife would help. So would evidence that they had lived together.","If Eira filed, she wanted to come out swinging with a case that could hold up in court.","An hour later, Luna Margaret arrived with Isabella.","Eira wasn’t surprised. Aside from Margaret, no one wanted that money back more than Isabella.","A faint handprint still marked Isabella’s cheek. She dropped into the chair and glared across the table.","When her eyes met Eira’s, something complicated crossed her face. Eira had once been the person she hated most. Now Isabella knew that Eira had been the one protecting her and the entire Hale Pack.","Serena, the woman Isabella had trusted, was the real con artist.","The truth made Isabella furious. At Serena. At Eira. At everyone except herself.","\"So you just let another woman blow through your husband’s money?\" she snapped. \"How useless can you be?\"","\"You spent all day sucking up to Serena and never noticed she was draining your brother’s account,\" Eira shot back. \"You weren’t smarter than me. You were just easier to fool.\"","Isabella’s jaw tightened. \"You little...\"","\"That’s enough.\" Luna Margaret caught her daughter by the arm. \"Both of you, knock it off.\"","She pulled out her phone and slid it across the table. \"You wanted video, so I recorded the entire text thread instead of taking screenshots. I saved the transfer records too. There’s nothing small or sentimental in them.\"","\"Sebastian doesn’t do small,\" Lila said. \"That man starts at six figures. He’d never leave a trail with some cute little payment.\"","Eira skimmed the recording and saved the useful sections to her phone. The file was too long to review at the table. Susan would have to go through the original before they used anything in court.","\"Send me the full recording,\" Eira said. \"Keep the original file.\"","Luna Margaret nodded, then looked at Isabella. \"Show her the rest.\"","Isabella opened her bag and pulled out six printed international flight itineraries.","\"I found them tucked under a drawer,\" Luna Margaret said. \"The print is faded, but I verified the booking numbers with the airline.\"","Isabella tapped the papers. \"Six years in a row. Serena’s birthday every time.\"","She looked at Eira, her voice sharp despite the swelling on her cheek. \"My mom and I have been busting our backs to find this stuff. You’d better get every dime back. That snake doesn’t get to walk away laughing.\"","Eira didn’t answer. She was still uploading the recording when Alpha Sebastian’s name flashed across her screen.","The call dropped.","A second later, he called again. Then again.","Luna Margaret glanced at the screen. \"I’ll take this.\"","She stepped outside before answering.","\"Why are you calling like the building’s on fire?\" Luna Margaret asked.","\"Mom...\" Alpha Sebastian began. He went quiet, then forced the words out.","\"Serena’s pregnant.\""]},{"number":163,"title":"Chapter 163 He Chooses Eira","paragraphs":["Eira and Lila watched Luna Margaret pace outside the diner with her phone pressed to her ear. Across the table, Isabella kept going on about the money like a broken record.","\"Are either of you even listening to me?\" Isabella snapped.","\"Nope,\" Lila said, not looking up. \"And nobody’s making me.\"","Isabella snatched the flight itineraries off the table. \"Unbelievable.\"","Eira ignored them. Her eyes stayed on Luna Margaret.","Her mother’s expression shifted from calm to stunned, then tense. She kept glancing back at their table as she listened, her brow drawing tighter by the second.","Something had happened.","Eira felt it in her gut.","When Luna Margaret finally came back, her voice was short and tense. \"We’ll deal with the evidence later. Something came up. Isabella, we’re leaving.\"","\"What? But the money...\"","Luna Margaret grabbed her daughter by the arm and pulled her toward the door before she could finish.","Lila blinked after them. \"She’s walking away from the money? Just like that?\"","Eira was already on her feet. \"We’re following them.\"","\"Already on it.\" Lila opened her rideshare app and requested a car. The moment Luna Margaret’s SUV pulled away, Lila gave the driver the address.","As they merged into traffic, Lila frowned at the road ahead. \"I don’t get it. Luna Margaret wants that money back more than she wants oxygen. What could possibly be more important?\"","Eira narrowed her eyes. That was exactly what bothered her.","Luna Margaret Hale treated money like most wolves treated territory. Whatever had pulled her away from the evidence had to be serious.","The rideshare followed Luna Margaret’s SUV to the edge of Hale Pack territory. Before they crossed the boundary, Eira told the driver to pull over.","There was no point following the Hales onto their own land. Their border patrols would spot them before they got close enough to learn anything useful.","\"Take us back,\" Eira said.","Lila looked disappointed. Then her expression brightened. \"What if I put a few people on the Hales? Just keep tabs on the family.\"","Eira nodded. \"Do it.\"","Lila pulled out her phone and started sending texts. \"I’ll have updates before they know they’re being watched.\"","--","Inside the Hale estate, Isabella pulled free the moment the door shut.","\"I thought we were working with Eira. Why did you bail on her? And what was with the secret-agent routine?\"","Luna Margaret’s palms were slick with sweat. She ignored the question.","\"Call your father. Tell him to come home. Now.\"","Isabella’s stomach dropped. \"Is the Pack in trouble?\"","\"It will be if you don’t make that call. Move.\"","Alpha Sebastian and Alpha Roger arrived within the hour, both looking grim.","Alpha Roger dropped into an armchair. \"All right. What’s going on?\"","Luna Margaret looked at Alpha Sebastian.","He pulled a folded medical report from his pocket and handed it to his father. His voice was low.","\"Serena’s pregnant.\"","Alpha Sebastian hated himself for losing control.","He hated himself even more for not warning Serena afterward.","He could still explain the money to Eira. But a pup was different.","Alpha Roger closed his eyes.","Isabella recovered first. Her shock quickly turned into suspicion. \"She gets pregnant the second we start coming after her for the money? That’s not suspicious at all.\"","\"What money?\" Alpha Roger asked.","Isabella went quiet. She had been told not to say anything.","Luna Margaret sighed. \"Eira has been building a case against Serena. She wants to recover the money Sebastian spent on her during the affair. \"","Alpha Sebastian’s eyes widened.","Alpha Roger’s frown deepened. \"I thought Eira said she wanted nothing from this family.\"","\"Nothing?\" Luna Margaret scoffed. \"Do you know how much Sebastian handed that woman? We’re just supposed to let hundreds of millions of dollars walk out the door?\"","\"So you joined forces with Eira to take Serena to court?\" Alpha Roger asked.","\"We’re not suing our own son. Relax.\" Luna Margaret rubbed her temple. \"And it doesn’t matter now. Serena is pregnant. I didn’t send Eira the evidence.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s head snapped up. \"What evidence?\"","Luna Margaret said nothing.","He already knew. She had gone through his phone.","His jaw tightened. \"Next time, talk to me before you go digging through my things.\"","\"Don’t pin this on me.\" Luna Margaret pointed at him. \"One minute you’re throwing money at Serena. The next, you’re chasing after Eira. No one in this house knows what you want anymore.\"","She stepped closer.","\"So pick, Sebastian. Serena and her baby, or Eira?\"","Then she turned to Alpha Roger. \"I say we keep the pup. Even if Eira comes back, she can’t give this Pack an heir. What good is a Luna who can’t continue the bloodline?\"","Alpha Roger hesitated. The Hale line could not end with him.","\"Eira can have pups,\" Alpha Sebastian said sharply, his voice carrying the Alpha’s authority.","\"Then why hasn’t she had one in four years?\" Luna Margaret shot back. \"And don’t blame yourself. If you were the problem, Serena wouldn’t be pregnant.\"","Alpha Sebastian opened his mouth, but no answer came.","Only he knew the truth. Eira had never conceived because he had never touched her. Not once. He had held himself back every time, convinced that Serena was his true mate.","But after Eira left, everything changed.","Without her in front of him, she filled his thoughts. Serena faded into the background while Eira became clearer, brighter, impossible to ignore. The bond he had rejected for four years finally forced its way to the surface.","\"Eira is the only woman I will ever call my mate,\" Alpha Sebastian said. Every word was firm.","Luna Margaret’s voice rose. \"And what about Serena’s baby?\"","\"Eira wants pups. She loves them.\" His voice faltered for the first time. \"I never gave her the chance.\"","The room fell silent.","Alpha Roger stared at him. Then his face hardened with fury.","\"You damned fool.\"","A pup would have tied Eira to the Hale Pack. She might never have left.","Her identity was already public now. If she had still been here, the Hale Pack could have claimed her as their Luna and enjoyed every advantage that came with her name.","But Alpha Sebastian had never given her a pup. He had kept her outside the Pack’s inner circle while Serena enjoyed its protection, money, and resources.","Alpha Roger’s expression darkened. \"You had a healthy mate under your roof for four years and never even tried to secure the bloodline?\"","Alpha Sebastian lowered his eyes. \"I was a fool. That’s why I’m done being one.\"","He looked at his parents.","\"Forget the money. Consider it Serena’s settlement.\"","Luna Margaret still looked uneasy. \"You can let it go, but Eira won’t. \""]},{"number":164,"title":"Chapter 164 Whose Weight Counts More","paragraphs":["Serena had the medical report printed before returning to the Celestia Residences. By the time she let herself into the penthouse, a satisfied smile had settled on her face.","She had won.","A pup could bind a mother to a Pack, but it could bind a father just as tightly. Alpha Sebastian might be cold toward her now, but he would never abandon his own bloodline.","The Hales thought they could take their money back?","They would think twice once she was carrying the Pack’s heir. From now on, they would be the ones paying for her medical care, housing, and security. Eira had nothing that could compete with that.","Serena had been Alpha Sebastian’s first love. She came from a respectable family. Now she was carrying his pup.","In Serena’s mind, that put her ahead of Eira.","But she needed to tell the right people first. Not someone who would spread the news all over town.","Ethan came to mind. He was Alpha Sebastian’s oldest friend.","Serena sent him a text.","[Ethan, you know Sebastian better than anyone. Hypothetically, if I were pregnant, would he make me terminate the pregnancy just because Eira is still his mate?]","Then she thought of her parents. If anyone could pressure Alpha Sebastian into taking responsibility, it would be them.","She ignored Alpha Sebastian’s order to stay put. After pulling on a hat, sunglasses, and a mask, she headed home.","Robert and Jennifer had taken time off because of the mess involving Alpha Victor and Serena. They were still in town when she arrived.","The moment Serena walked through the door, both of them froze. She rarely visited. She always claimed their house looked nothing like her grandfather’s estate.","Then Jennifer noticed the hat, mask, and sunglasses. Her expression changed.","\"What happened?\" she asked, hurrying over.","She removed the disguise and found no injury on Serena’s face. A closer look revealed bruises behind her ear, along her neck, and across the backs of her wrists.","Robert’s face tightened. \"Did someone hurt you?\"","Serena dropped onto the couch. \"I’m thirsty.\"","Jennifer fetched her a glass of water while Robert watched with growing irritation. That helpless-princess routine had always gotten under his skin.","\"You were attacked,\" he said.","Serena had not expected him to figure it out so quickly, but she only waved him off. \"It’s nothing. I came to tell you something.\"","She pulled out the report and placed it on the coffee table.","\"I’m pregnant.\"","Robert picked up the report with shaking hands. \"Is it Alpha Sebastian’s? Serena, he’s still bonded to another woman. He already has a Luna.\"","\"Robert, let her explain.\" Jennifer put a hand on his arm.","\"It’s his. I’m four weeks pregnant.\" Serena looked from one parent to the other. \"You’re going to be grandparents. Aren’t you happy?\"","If Serena had been mated and settled, they would have been thrilled. Instead, she was carrying the pup of another wolf’s bonded mate.","Robert felt humiliated. Jennifer could barely speak.","\"I’m keeping this pup,\" Serena said. \"I’m not bringing a pup into the world without a Pack name or legal protection. You need to talk to the Hales.\"","She leaned back and stared at them.","\"I’m your only daughter. You were barely there when I was growing up, and you hardly helped me. Now that you’re finally here, you’re going to stand by me, right?\"","Neither of them had expected such cold words from their own daughter.","Jennifer steadied Robert, then sat across from Serena.","\"Sweetheart, hear me out.\" Her voice stayed gentle. \"Alpha Sebastian’s mate is Dr. Crawford. Unless Eira files to dissolve the bond, Alpha Sebastian won’t be able to do it himself. If he planned to leave Eira, he would have done it already.\"","Serena’s fingers tightened around the report.","Jennifer continued, \"A pup conceived outside a recognized bond may not have standing in a Pack. That means no Pack protection, no inheritance claim, and no guaranteed place in the bloodline.\"","She reached across the table.\"Serena, we’re not going to pretend this is simple.\"","\"You have options,\" Jennifer continued. \"You can continue the pregnancy, make an adoption plan, or terminate it while you’re still early. We can schedule a private appointment and...\"","Serena let out a cold laugh.\"I’m keeping the baby.\"","\"Then what do you think marrying Alpha Sebastian will get you?\" Jennifer asked, her voice softening with something close to grief. \"Be honest.\"","\"Status. Money. Territory. And years of history.\" Serena did not hesitate. \"Grandfather said he’d help me start over once this mess blows over. If Sebastian and I bond, two powerful bloodlines will join the same Pack. That is a real alliance.\"","In the wolf world, a powerful bloodline meant more than a family name. It meant stronger alliances, greater control over territory, and more wolves willing to fight under the same banner.","A Pack’s land provided hunting grounds, homes, and safe places for its pregnant females and young pups.","So Alpha Victor planned to keep bankrolling her.","Jennifer opened her mouth, then let out a tired breath.","\"I’m your daughter,\" Serena pressed. \"You were always working. You were never around, and you never did anything for me. Now that you’re finally here, are you really going to turn your back on me?\"","The guilt landed exactly where she wanted it to.","No matter how reasonable a parent was, cutting off their own pup was not easy.","In the end, Jennifer and Robert gave in.","\"If Alpha Sebastian refuses to bond with you and you still want to keep the baby, we’ll help,\" Jennifer said quietly. \"We can raise the pup with you.\"","\"Why would he refuse?\"","Serena’s expression hardened. She did not believe Alpha Sebastian could abandon his own pup. The Hale Pack would never willingly let an Alpha’s heir slip away, either.","With her parents on her side, Serena called Alpha Sebastian.","She softened her voice, adding just enough hurt to make him feel guilty.\"Sebastian, my parents know about the baby. They want to meet you.\"","Alpha Sebastian already had a pounding headache. Serena’s pregnancy had blindsided him that morning. That afternoon, he had learned that his mother and Isabella were working with Eira to recover the money. By nightfall, he was dealing with the move.","Now the Winthrops wanted a family meeting.He had been careless, so he could hardly blame them for wanting answers.","\"When?\"","\"Whenever you’re free.\"","\"Give me a few days. I have a Pack summit tomorrow, followed by business dinners.\"","\"Okay.\" Serena paused. \"Sebastian, the doctor said it was lucky yesterday’s injuries didn’t hit my stomach.\"","His brow furrowed, but he said nothing.","\"Our pup is a fighter,\" she added softly. \"Go take care of business. We’ll be thinking about you.\"","Her voice no longer had much power over him.","Then she said our pup.","His first pup.","The thought caught him off guard.","Isabella was the only one in the family who had not softened at the news.","His mother still did not want Serena anywhere near the Hale estate after what she had done with the money, but she could not bear the thought of losing an heir.","His father believed Serena was no match for Eira and wanted no part of her in the Pack. But he also refused to let the Hale bloodline die out.","They had argued in circles and still had no answer."]},{"number":165,"title":"Chapter 165 Borrowing Her Name","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian had never been the kind of Alpha who dealt with household details.","His father had led the Hale Pack while Alpha Sebastian was growing up.","Once Alpha Sebastian became strong enough to take over, the Pack had fallen in line behind him.","After bonding with Eira, he buried himself in Hale Group business while she quietly handled everything else. Household matters. Pack disputes. The endless small problems that never made it to his desk.","Lately, those problems had become his responsibility.","They wore him down more than border disputes or territory talks ever had.","With Eira around, life had been easy. He had only needed to lead. She had taken care of the rest.","He missed her.","Before he could think better of it, he found himself walking toward Number Nine.","He had barely made it halfway up the driveway when he spotted two of Alpha Killian’s guards beside the front gate. Each man held the leash of a massive German shepherd.","Alpha Sebastian slowed.","The guards noticed him at once. They stopped, turned the dogs toward him, and let the animals see exactly who was approaching.","\"Woof!\"","The second dog joined in.","The barking tore through the quiet evening. Alpha Sebastian’s brow tightened. He took one step toward the gate.","The guards took one step toward him.","The shepherds lunged against their leashes, barking and baring their teeth.","This was no coincidence. Someone had placed them there to keep him away.","Alpha Killian’s idea?","Lila’s?","Or Eira’s?","Every possibility made Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tighten.","\"Ei...\" he began.","The guards loosened the leashes.","Alpha Sebastian turned around and walked away.","--","Inside Number Nine, Mrs. Jones opened the front door when she heard the barking. She saw the guards standing by the gate and Alpha Sebastian’s retreating figure. Nothing looked out of control, so she closed the door and went back to ironing.","When she finished, she found Eira stretching beside the desk near the window.","\"Miss Crawford, tomorrow’s outfit is pressed and ready.\"","\"Thank you, Mrs. Jones.\"","Eira went to bed early. She had more important things to deal with than the aftermath of cutting Alpha Sebastian out of her life.","The Sovereign Processor Initiative would officially launch the next morning.","Alpha Killian had presented the project himself at the procurement summit. The processor would support three major sectors: defense, agriculture, and industry.","The Pack Council was watching the project closely. Reliable energy meant stronger defenses, better food production, and more control over Pack territory. It also meant the Hales would no longer have to depend entirely on human power suppliers.","For smaller and more remote Packs that still relied on the human grid to power their border systems, the technology could mean the difference between survival and losing their land.","Three hundred engineers had been divided into three teams.","Professor Davies led the industrial division, while Claire headed agriculture.","Eira worked with the defense team, officially as an assistant. In reality, she shared top-level oversight with Sterling’s Director of Research and Development, George, and Alpha Killian himself.","Three divisions. Three project leads. Separate authority, with built-in checks and balances.","There would be no public launch or press event—not yet. Until the final processor was ready, the entire project would remain strictly confidential.","Each division had its own entrance and iris scanner, and team members were not permitted to move between facilities without clearance.","Only Eira, Alpha Killian, and George had unrestricted access to all three divisions.","Lila had been assigned to the defense team. Sterling heiress or not, star protégé or not, she was still junior enough to spend her time logging test results and cleaning up data.","She didn’t care. She was happy to be there.","--","Across town, Alpha Sebastian heard about the launch. He set his work aside and looked at Beta Jordan.","\"Any media coverage?\"","Beta Jordan pulled up Sterling Industries’ website on his tablet. \"One group photo and a short press release.\"","The photo showed engineers, researchers, and several young wolves from Pack families. Alpha Sebastian barely noticed them. His eyes went straight to Eira, standing in the center of the front row.","Alpha Killian stood beside her.","Of course he did.","Alpha Sebastian clenched his jaw. That project should have been his. So should the place beside Eira. Alpha Killian had taken everything from him.","He pushed the tablet away. \"Get Finn. We’re meeting with Snowmark’s representative.\"","They met in an ultra-private dining room, where Beta Jordan had arranged dinner, drinks, and the kind of discreet, polished service expected at a high-level business meeting.","After a few rounds of cocktails, Alpha Sebastian brought the conversation back to business. He placed the proposal and contract on the table.","Soren, Snowmark’s executive, had already reviewed the proposal. Otherwise, he would never have agreed to the meeting. The deal should have been straightforward.","But Soren still hesitated. He clearly wasn’t convinced that Hale Group had enough influence to handle the partnership. Instead of signing, he brought up the American-made processor that had recently appeared and shaken up the entire industry.","Finn and Beta Jordan exchanged a quick look.","Does he know we lost the bid?","Alpha Sebastian asked a few careful questions and soon understood what was going on. Soren had not heard the result of the procurement process. He had only heard the rumors surrounding the Sovereign Processor Initiative.","An idea came to Alpha Sebastian.","\"Soren,\" he said, \"the initiative you mentioned is being led by my wife, Dr. Eira Crawford.\"","He pulled up Eira’s feature article on his phone. Then he opened a photo from his wedding and placed the phone beside the proposal.","Soren’s hesitation disappeared.","If Eira was truly leading the project and was married to Alpha Sebastian, then Hale Group had a direct connection to the technology. At least, that was the conclusion Soren drew.","Soren stood and extended his hand.","\"It’s a pleasure doing business with you, Mr. Hale.\""]},{"number":166,"title":"Chapter 166 Circling Wolves","paragraphs":["Once Snowmark’s representative left, Finn’s easy smile vanished. He shot Alpha Sebastian a cold look, then walked away without saying a word.","Alpha Sebastian didn’t react.","Jordan hesitated. \"What’s wrong with Finn Carter?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened. \"He’s a lovesick pup. Nothing to worry about.\"","A lovesick pup who’d just had it made painfully clear that the woman he’d been chasing for days was Alpha Sebastian’s mate.","Alpha Sebastian glanced at the contract in Jordan’s hand, a faint smile touching his lips.\"It doesn’t matter. With Snowmark on board and Dr. Shaw’s patents behind us, the board will stop hounding me over the processor bid.\"","Jordan nodded. \"There’s one more problem. Dr. Shaw still hasn’t returned our calls.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression darkened. If they couldn’t secure the patents soon, the year-end business rush would make everything more difficult.","\"Find out his schedule, then arrange a meeting. What does he like?\"","\"He collects antique furniture. There’s an upcoming auction with a rare set of hand-carved rosewood chairs from the colonial era. The date hasn’t been announced yet.\"","\"Keep watching. We can’t miss our chance.\"","\"I’ll handle it.\" Jordan paused, choosing his next words carefully. \"There’s one other issue. Alpha, you need to rein in your spending. You’ve already used more than eighty percent of your available cash this month. If we don’t slow down, you won’t have enough left for the chairs or the favors we’ll need to call in before the end of the year.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened.","He knew his money was disappearing fast. Serena’s apartment, car, and jewelry. Eira’s clothes and bags. The rental payment he had made without a second thought.","\"Go back to the office,\" he said. \"I have personal business to deal with tonight.\"","After Jordan left, Alpha Sebastian called Ethan.","\"Come have a drink with me.\"","Ethan had been waiting for days to question Alpha Sebastian about Eira’s identity and Serena’s situation. By the time he arrived at the bar, he was practically bursting with questions.","They took a booth in the corner and clinked glasses. Alpha Sebastian drained half his drink in one swallow. Ethan barely touched his before leaning across the table.","\"Is it true? Eira really is the chief engineer of the Sovereign Processor Initiative? It’s right there on Sterling Industries’ official website. They wouldn’t fake something like that.\"","\"You said it yourself. It’s on the official website.\" Alpha Sebastian poured himself another drink. The shifting bar lights made his expression hard to read. \"That kind of thing can’t be faked.\"","\"I thought I was losing my mind. The Eira we know and the woman leading that project are completely different people. The difference is insane.\"","\"Watch your tone.\" Alpha Sebastian suddenly looked up.","\"Right. Your Luna.\" Ethan raised both hands. \"But you’ve always said you wanted a woman who stood out. Eira is exactly that now. She’s brilliant, capable, and all over the news. So what are you going to do about Serena?\"","Alpha Sebastian fell silent.","He poured another drink and finished it.","Then he said, \"Serena’s pregnant.\"","At that exact moment, the music on the dance floor stopped.","A couple passing near the booth caught every word. When they heard Serena’s name, Fiona grabbed Barry’s arm and pulled him back.","The bar was packed, and Sebastian was too deep in his own problems to notice them.","\"Pregnant?\" Ethan set down his glass. \"What are you going to do? You can’t keep her hidden forever.\"","A thought crossed his mind. \"You’re not planning to ask her to terminate the pregnancy, are you?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression hardened. \"It’s a life. It’s my blood.\"","Ethan let out a slow breath. \"Then what happens to Eira?\"","\"You don’t even like Eira,\" he said. \"Let her go. Marry Serena. You get the woman you wanted and the baby. Simple.\"","Alpha Sebastian answered without hesitation.","\"The woman I want is Eira.\"","Ethan stared at him. \"Come again? Every time I asked if you had feelings for her, you shut me down. Now you’re doing a complete one-eighty?\"","\"I didn’t understand my own heart.\" Alpha Sebastian met his eyes. \"I spent four years with Eira. We were happy. You can’t honestly say we weren’t.\"","[You were happy,] Ethan thought. [Whether Eira was happy is another question.]","Alpha Sebastian saw the silence on his face and did not try to defend himself.","\"I treated her terribly. I’ll make it right. My parents and Isabella won’t touch her again. I’ll give her control of the finances. All of them. We’ll have a pup. Maybe two.\"","\"And Serena’s baby?\" Ethan cut in. \"You’re losing me here.\"","\"It was an accident!\" Alpha Sebastian’s voice rose. \"The pregnancy wasn’t planned.\"","Ethan rubbed his forehead.","\"So you’ve realized Eira is your Luna, and you refuse to let her go. Fine. But you still have to decide what you’re doing about Serena and the baby. Keep dragging this out, and it will blow up in your face. I’m telling you straight, brother.\"","Alpha Sebastian stared into his glass. \"Either Serena keeps the pregnancy and stays out of sight, or she doesn’t go through with it at all.\"","Ethan raised his glass. \"So you still haven’t made a real decision.\"","He had always thought he was the reckless one, moving from woman to woman without getting caught. Apparently, Alpha Sebastian had him beat.","\"Here. Drink until your problems pass out before you do.\"","Across the room, Fiona nudged Barry.","\"Come on. Logan’s waiting.\"","Barry smirked. \"One story for the public and another behind closed doors. Guess your father misjudged him.\"","\"Don’t start,\" Fiona snapped.","\"Want me to warn him?\" Barry nodded toward Alpha Sebastian. \"That guy is a walking disaster. Keeping him close sounds like a terrible idea.\"","Fiona said nothing. She had no control over who her father kept on the payroll. If he knew what Alpha Sebastian was capable of and still protected him, he had his reasons.","Her phone buzzed.","It was Finn.","\"Fiona, Sebastian’s mate is Eira? He has Eira and he’s still sneaking around with Serena? What kind of idiot does that?\"","\"I know Eira is his mate. Why are you freaking out?\"","Then she paused.","\"Wait. Don’t tell me Eira is your dream girl.\"","Barry’s head turned sharply at the name.","He shook his head. \"Forget it. Alpha Killian is already circling her. He’s guarding that territory like a wolf over a fresh kill. Your golden boy doesn’t stand a chance.\"","Fiona had seen it herself on the yacht. But she had no intention of letting her brother back down.","\"Go after her, Finn. If you win Eira, I’ll turn your confession into the event of the year.\"","Barry stared at her.","Then he quietly pulled out his phone and typed a message.","[Alpha Killian, don’t say I didn’t warn you. Finn Carter is pursuing Miss Crawford.]","He started another line.","[One more thing. Serena...]","Fiona snatched the phone from his hand before he could finish."]},{"number":167,"title":"Chapter 167 The Strongest Evidence","paragraphs":["These days, Eira’s life came down to three things: the Sovereign Processor Initiative, renovating Number Nine, and working with Susan to recover the assets Alpha Sebastian had taken from her.","Her schedule left no time for brooding, which suited her just fine.","So when Alpha Killian offered her a ride back to Southridge Estates, she thanked him and climbed into the SUV. Lila slipped in right after her.","Alpha Killian gave his sister a flat look. \"You have your own place.\"","\"I’m staying for a few days,\" Lila said. \"My thesis is due in March, and I need Eira to review it.\"","On the drive back, Eira worked on her tablet. She uploaded photos of Number Nine into a home-design app, then added flooring samples, furniture, light fixtures, and paint colors.","The layout was rough and a little chaotic, but it showed exactly what she wanted.","\"No designer?\" Alpha Killian asked.","\"Once I finish the layout, I’ll know what I actually like.\" She didn’t look up. \"That’ll make the meeting easier.\"","Alpha Killian grunted and let her work.","A moment later, her phone began buzzing inside her coat pocket.","\"Your phone,\" he said.","Eira didn’t hear him.","He leaned slightly closer. \"Eira, your phone’s ringing.\"","She turned toward him. Their eyes met for half a second.","His gaze moved over her face, paused at her lips, then shifted away.","Eira pulled out her phone.","She set the tablet facedown on her lap and straightened.","\"Dr. Shaw.\"","The caller was Adrian Shaw, an old friend of her mentor who had always looked out for her.","\"Eira, you’re free Friday night, correct?\"","\"I am. I haven’t forgotten.\"","\"Good.\"","The call ended.","Lila leaned over immediately. \"Dr. Shaw? The Dr. Shaw? The one people mention in the same breath as Dr. Thorne?\"","Eira nodded.","Alpha Killian’s eyes flickered. \"Sebastian’s meeting with Dr. Shaw. Did you arrange that?\"","\"Not exactly. I mentioned his name once. The old man remembered.\"","What she left unsaid was that Dr. Shaw remembered because he cared about her, sharp temper and all.","Eira clearly had no interest in discussing Alpha Sebastian, so Alpha Killian changed the subject.","\"What did Dr. Shaw want?\"","\"His birthday dinner,\" Eira said, her voice softening automatically. \"On Friday.\"","\"That can’t be right.\" Lila frowned. \"Every bio online says his birthday is next Tuesday.\"","\"That’s the point.\" Eira smiled faintly. \"He always celebrates on the Friday before. By his actual birthday, he’s gone. Anyone looking for a favor has no chance of tracking him down.\"","Lila’s jaw dropped. \"Professor Chase has been promising to introduce me to him for three years. Now I know why he never came through.\"","\"He’s an acquired taste.\"","Even Dr. Alaric Thorne had struggled to pin Dr. Shaw down.","The two old men had often used her as a go-between, sending messages through her when neither could be bothered to deal with the other directly.","Those months of running back and forth between two brilliant minds had taught her more than any textbook.","A faint shadow crossed her face.","Dr. Thorne had always chosen Dr. Shaw’s birthday gift.","Now that he was gone, Eira found herself wondering what on earth she was supposed to get Dr. Shaw.","Alpha Killian noticed the change in her expression.","\"Miles looked into it,\" he said. \"Dr. Shaw collects antique furniture. There’s an auction tomorrow night with something he’d want.\"","\"Then you should go with my brother, Eira,\" Lila said quickly. \"I can’t make it.\"","She absolutely could have made it. She simply refused to let Alpha Killian remain single forever and then have the entire family blame her for it.","Eira had some money now. Not enough to spend freely, but enough to buy a proper gift.","She nodded. \"All right.\"","When they reached Number Nine, two German shepherds trotted over as soon as Eira stepped out of the SUV, their tails wagging.","The dogs had recently joined the estate’s security detail. They were trained alongside the Pack sentries who patrolled the tree line and monitored the surrounding roads. Whenever they caught an unfamiliar scent, they alerted the guards.","Eira crouched and scratched behind their ears.","\"Duke. Scout.\"","The dogs leaned into her hands while she played with them for a few minutes. Then she went inside with Alpha Killian and Lila.","Not long after, the dogs began barking again.","A familiar voice came from the entryway.","\"When did you get guard dogs?\" Barry asked. \"What are you protecting this place from?\"","He glanced at the two sentries standing beside the door. Their Pack insignias and rigid posture made their roles obvious, even though Barry had never seen them before.","\"Is Miss Crawford back?\" he asked. \"Is Alpha Killian here?\"","The sentries remained silent.","Barry had spotted Alpha Killian’s SUV, so he reached for his phone.","Before he could make the call, Eira appeared with Alpha Killian close behind her, his imposing presence looming at her back like the biggest guard dog on the property.","\"Come on in, Dr. Wood,\" Eira said.","Barry stepped inside, rubbing his temples and wincing. Alpha Killian took one look at him and knew he was hungover.","Mrs. Jones poured him a glass of water. Barry drank half of it before getting to the point.","\"I tried texting you last night, Alpha, but the message wouldn’t go through. I figured I’d save myself the trouble and tell you in person.\"","Lila blinked. \"How did you know he’d be here?\"","Barry spread his hands. \"Where else would he be?\"","Lila nodded. Her brother had practically become Number Nine’s resident ghost.","Barry glanced at Eira. \"Since Miss Crawford is here, I’ll just say it. Serena’s pregnant. I overheard it at the bar last night.\"","\"Pregnant?\" Lila’s face tightened. \"Why would you drop that on Eira?\"","\"About four weeks, if I heard him right,\" Barry added.","Eira’s expression remained calm.","\"Four weeks,\" she repeated softly. \"Then it happened during the mandatory separation period.\"","Lila and Mrs. Jones immediately moved to her sides and took her hands, their faces filled with sympathy.","Eira gave them a faint smile. \"I’m fine. Dr. Wood just brought us exactly what we needed.\"","Mrs. Jones’s eyes turned red. \"Exactly what we needed? Your divorce from Mr. Hale wasn’t even final yet!\"","Certain that Eira was in denial, Lila pulled her into a hug.","Eira gently patted her arm. \"We were missing one solid piece of evidence, weren’t we? That baby is the key.\"","Alpha Killian looked at her, quiet approval warming his eyes.","\"As far as I know, the divorce waiting period doesn’t end the marriage. Legally, you were still married.\""]},{"number":168,"title":"Chapter 168 A Close Call","paragraphs":["Lila’s eyes widened. \"Right. The baby changes everything.\"","Then she frowned. \"But how do we prove it? Barry, why didn’t you record Sebastian last night?\"","\"Because we were in a crowded bar, not a courtroom.\" Barry took another drink of water. \"A shaky phone recording gives their lawyers plenty of room to argue. We need Serena’s medical records. The clinic can confirm the pregnancy and the timeline.\"","\"So the one piece of evidence we need is the one they’ll keep under lock and key.\"","\"Now you’re catching on.\"","Eira’s expression turned thoughtful. \"They won’t hand it over. Sebastian will hide Serena somewhere private. He’ll want the baby.\"","\"Why?\" Alpha Killian asked.","The question slipped out before he could stop it.","Alpha Sebastian was not stupid. If Serena’s pregnancy timeline placed the conception during the divorce proceedings, it could become powerful evidence against him. Hiding her should have been the obvious move.","Then Alpha Killian saw Eira’s face.","Her lashes lowered, and something in his chest tightened.","Four years married to Alpha Sebastian. Not one pup. Serena had been back for barely a month and was already carrying his heir.","\"You don’t have to answer,\" Alpha Killian said.","\"There’s nothing to explain.\" Eira looked at them calmly. \"Sebastian wanted children with Serena. As it turned out, that’s why I never had a pup during our marriage.\"","The crystal tumbler in Alpha Killian’s hand shattered.","Everyone went silent.","Blood ran down his palm. The air in the room turned cold as his wolf pushed against his control.","Eira stared at his hand. \"Alpha?\"","Mrs. Jones recovered first. \"Cheap glass. I knew those things were a bad buy.\" She pointed at Barry. \"First-aid kit. Now.\"","Barry grabbed it.","\"I’ll do it,\" Eira said.","She reached for Alpha Killian’s hand.","He caught her wrist. \"There’s a couch right there.\"","Eira looked at him. \"Are you giving me furniture advice?\"","\"I’m telling you not to kneel on the floor.\"","\"I’m not made of glass.\"","\"Apparently, glass is the problem in this house.\"","Barry turned away to hide a laugh. Lila did not bother hiding hers.","Alpha Killian released Eira’s wrist. The moment he did, she sat on the couch and opened the first-aid kit.","\"Hand.\"","\"I can take the glass out myself.\"","\"Great. You can do that after I clean the wound.\"","Alpha Killian took the tweezers with his uninjured hand. Eira disinfected his palm, and he removed the shards one by one.","When he finished, he held out his hand.","Eira applied ointment and wrapped the cuts in gauze. Alpha Killian almost objected, then saw her expression and thought better of it.","\"Try not to break anything else,\" she said.","\"I’ll do my best.\"","\"Your best is not very reassuring.\"","His mouth twitched.","Lila leaned toward Barry. \"Is this what passes for flirting in Alpha country?\"","Barry whispered back, \"Apparently.\"","Alpha Killian shot them both a warning look. They immediately became fascinated by the first-aid kit.","He pulled out his phone.","\"Hey, Siri. Call Kate.\"","\"Alpha.\"","\"Keep watch on every hospital, clinic, and private women’s health center in Palo Alto. If anyone spots Serena or Sebastian, follow them and report back. I want to know where she goes.\"","\"Got it. Miles has also been sending updates from overseas.\"","\"Tell him to dig deeper. Find out which clinic Serena is using.\"","The call ended.","Eira finished wrapping his hand. \"Just one layer. I didn’t want it getting in your way.\"","\"Mm.\"","Alpha Killian watched her lowered lashes tremble as she secured the gauze.","She looked up with a faint smile. \"You’ve done all this for me, Killian. What do you want in return?\"","The room went quiet.","Everyone waited for his answer.","Alpha Killian met her clear, trusting gaze and remembered his mother’s warning.","She’s been hurt badly. Don’t rush her.","\"I want you fully committed to the Sovereign Processor Initiative,\" he said. His voice stayed calm, but his gaze never left hers. \"Get the defense, agricultural, and industrial systems ready for market. Move fast.\"","Eira held his stare. \"I’ll deliver on schedule.\"","\"Good.\"","Alpha Killian glanced at his bandaged hand, then nodded toward Barry.","\"Walk with me.\"","They had barely stepped outside the gate when Barry grinned.","\"In a hurry, Alpha? Afraid you’d blow your cover if you stayed another minute?\"","Alpha Killian ignored him.","He had kept the conversation strictly professional for one reason. He did not want Eira to think she owed him anything.","The two men left the property.","--","When Luna Margaret heard that Alpha Sebastian was meeting with the Winthrops, she insisted on coming.","\"Serena has both her parents backing her,\" she told Alpha Sebastian. \"You don’t think I’m going to let them corner you alone, do you?\"","By the time everyone arrived, both families were seated around the same table.","Robert and Jennifer finally got a close look at the Alpha their daughter had sacrificed everything for.","Robert looked at the Hales as though they were beneath him.","Luna Margaret sat perfectly straight, her chin raised. Her daughter had made the mess, so why should Luna Margaret be the one squirming?","Alpha Sebastian felt heat creep up his neck under the older couple’s scrutiny.","He had never imagined a night like this. Two sets of parents facing each other across a dinner table like rival Alphas negotiating over a border."]},{"number":169,"title":"Chapter 169 No Shame","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian played the perfect host, refilling everyone’s wineglasses with practiced ease.","\"Mr. and Mrs. Winthrop.\"","Robert and Jennifer had no interest in small talk. Luna Margaret, however, sipped her wine as if she owned the table.","Jennifer got straight to the point. \"Mr. Hale, you know my daughter is pregnant. How does the Hale Pack plan to handle this? A Winthrop woman will not carry a pup for an Alpha who refuses to claim her.\"","Alpha Sebastian started to answer, but Luna Margaret cut in with a sharp smile.","\"Are you using the baby as leverage? Both of them made their own choices. But if you think Serena’s pregnancy earns her a place in this Pack, think again. The Hale Pack has one Luna, and that is Eira. What exactly does Serena bring to the table?\"","Serena sat stiffly, her hands clenched in her lap. Her eyes flashed with anger.","Robert shoved back his chair. \"How dare you speak about my daughter like that?\"","Luna Margaret did not flinch.","Robert turned to Jennifer and Serena. \"We’re leaving. If you want to keep the baby, Serena, your mother and I will support you.\"","\"Sit down,\" Luna Margaret said when Alpha Sebastian began to rise.","Serena looked at him with wounded eyes.","He said nothing.","Jennifer pulled Robert back into his chair. Luna Margaret did the same to Alpha Sebastian.","\"Aunt Margaret ,\" Serena said softly, \"I’m carrying Hale blood. Haven’t you always wanted an heir from Sebastian?\"","Luna Margaret took another sip of wine.","\"We want the baby.\"","Hope brightened Serena’s face.","\"But if you keep it, the Pack will not give you the Hale name, the Luna title, or any claim to Pack status. If you can accept that, the Hales will be grateful.\"","\"Shameless!\" Robert slammed his hand on the table. He turned to Alpha Sebastian. \"You’re the Alpha. Do you have a backbone, or are you going to sit there and let them treat her like this?\"","Alpha Sebastian had spent the previous night drinking until he could no longer think. By morning, his head was clear, and so was his decision.","He did not want this baby.","One day, he and Eira would have heirs of their own. Their pups would carry the Hale bloodline and belong to a true bond.","\"I owe you both an apology,\" Alpha Sebastian said calmly. \"We’re adults, and we’re responsible for our own choices. But I will not continue this pregnancy.\"","The words left a dull ache in his chest. This would have been his first pup.","Serena stared at him. \"Sebastian, what are you saying?\"","\"This pregnancy puts everyone at risk,\" he said. \"Eira is preparing to claim her share of the marital and Pack assets. If she files, the baby will be clear proof that we had an affair during the separation.\"","Serena’s lips parted, then pressed together.She knew he was right.","Robert and Jennifer knew Alpha Sebastian had spent a fortune on their daughter. They had overlooked one important detail. Much of that money came from marital and Pack funds.","Now they sat there in silence, humiliated but unable to deny the truth.","Robert still refused to abandon Serena.","\"Fine,\" he said through clenched teeth. \"Then she won’t keep the baby.\"","Jennifer placed a hand on Serena’s arm. \"Sweetheart, think about the option I mentioned. You’re still early. You can start over.\"","Serena pulled away.","\"Never.\" Her eyes hardened. \"Sebastian, are you really willing to turn your back on your own child?\"","He was silent for a moment.","\"We’ll settle everything from the past,\" he said. \"I’ll even convince Eira to drop her claim to the marital assets.\"","Tears filled Serena’s eyes.","Alpha Sebastian was walking away and leaving her to deal with the fallout alone.","She took a breath. \"Give me time. You may not want this pup, but I do. It’s mine. It’s ours. Just give me time to think.\"","Alpha Sebastian nodded. \"Fine. Keep a low profile. We’ll stay out of each other’s way.\"","He turned to her parents. \"I’m sorry.\"","Robert and Jennifer looked away.","Luna Margaret’s expression turned cold. \"Don’t act like my son is the only one at fault. He spent millions on Serena. She used his money to buy her way into this family, kept everyone in the dark, then convinced Isabella to drug Eira and leave her with a stranger.\"","Robert and Jennifer went pale.","\"Isabella ended up in a holding cell,\" Luna Margaret continued. \"If Sebastian hadn’t kept quiet because of their history, Serena would have been the one facing charges. So don’t forget who protected her.\"","Serena looked ready to flip the table.","Luna Margaret stood. \"Sebastian, we’re leaving.\"","In the car, she weighed the situation. If Serena kept the baby, Luna Margaret would stay out of the asset dispute. If she didn’t, Luna Margaret would help Eira recover every dollar.","Either way, the Hale Pack would come out ahead.","Alpha Sebastian stared out the window. Walking away from his first pup hurt more than he wanted to admit.","\"Go home first, Mom.\"","\"Going back to comfort Serena?\"","\"No. I have an auction to prepare for.\"","He needed enough liquid cash in one account to pass the auction house’s proof-of-funds check. The rosewood armchair was expected to sell for up to two million dollars, but he planned to show access to $2.8 million.","--","The next evening, Alpha Sebastian and Jordan took their seats at the auction. They did not notice Alpha Killian and Eira watching from a private box above.","Kate leaned toward Alpha Killian. \"Hale brought proof of funds for $2.8 million.\"","Alpha Killian smiled. \"Almost broke. You know what to do.\"","Kate picked up a bidding paddle and headed downstairs.","Jordan spotted her first. \"Alpha, Alpha Killian is here. Second-floor box.\"","Alpha Sebastian followed his gaze. \"We’re here for the chair. Don’t let them distract you.\"The auction began.","The first lot was the antique rosewood armchair. The auctioneer opened at $450,000.","Jordan raised his paddle.","\"Five hundred thousand.\"","Kate lifted hers without hesitation.","\"Five-fifty.\"","Jordan froze.","So much for coincidence."]},{"number":170,"title":"Chapter 170 The Auction Trap","paragraphs":["The bidding opened with six paddles in the air.","Once the price passed one million dollars, most of them dropped out.","A few bidders tried to stay in, only to get an elbow from the wolf sitting beside them.","Two paddles remained.","One belonged to Jordan. The other belonged to Kate.","They raised the price in $50,000 increments, each refusing to back down.","Jordan raised the bid to $1.05 million.","Kate answered with $1.1 million.","At $1.5 million, Jordan leaned toward Alpha Sebastian. \"Alpha, we should stop. She’s only driving up the price.\"","Sebastian’s jaw tightened. \"What are the odds Alpha Killian actually wants the chance to meet Dr. Shaw? Give me the honest answer. Business and personal.\"","\"Business-wise, Sterling has the deepest pockets on the West Coast. Its territory is secure, its borders are well protected, and it has more than enough funding. The chair itself means nothing to them.\"","Jordan lowered his voice.","\"Personally, Alpha Killian wants Eira. He’ll block you whenever he gets the chance.\"","\"So?\"","\"Fifty-fifty.\"","Alpha Sebastian raised his own paddle.","\"One point six million.\"","He could not afford to lose his chance with Dr. Shaw. His position at Hale Group was already unstable, and he had planned to visit Dr. Shaw in person on Friday with a gift in hand.","He needed access to that patent.","Kate looked back at him and gave him a bright, poisonous smile.","\"One point seven.\"","In the private box upstairs, Alpha Killian watched Eira finish her third glass of water. She stared at the auction floor as if she were watching a hostage negotiation.","Apparently, getting a meeting with Dr. Shaw cost millions.","Alpha Killian let out a quiet laugh.","Eira turned toward him. \"Are you trying to meet Dr. Shaw too?\"","\"Are you offering to introduce me?\"","She paused. \"Someone with your reputation shouldn’t need an introduction.\"","\"You’d be surprised.\"","He leaned back in his chair.","\"I don’t care about the chair. It’s just an ordinary antique. Not my style.\"","Downstairs, the bidding passed two million dollars.","\"Two point two,\" Kate called.","Jordan’s forehead began to shine with sweat. A few million dollars had once meant nothing to Hale Group. After Alpha Sebastian’s recent spending spree, the company’s cash reserves were under serious pressure.","\"I want Sebastian’s accounts drained,\" Alpha Killian said.","Eira looked at him. \"Why?\"","\"When you win the asset case, will Sebastian still be responsible for Serena’s expenses?\"","\"He will be.\"","The plan clicked into place.","Alpha Killian’s smile turned cold. \"Then he needs money to pay those expenses. Once his accounts are empty, Serena is on her own. I doubt she can support herself for long.\"","Eira studied him. \"Thank you, Killian.\"","\"Deliver the project on schedule, and we’re even.\"","He glanced at her.","\"Although, dinner only covered the first favor. You owe me one now.\"","Behind them, Natalie pressed her lips together to keep from laughing. Alpha Killian was working awfully hard for a man who claimed he wanted nothing from Eira.","\"How do you know Sebastian will keep bidding?\" Eira asked.","\"Without Dr. Shaw’s patent, he may lose his position at Hale Group. He knows this auction is a trap, but he can’t walk away.\"","The bidding climbed again.","\"Two point six,\" Kate said.","Alpha Sebastian’s face went dark. He raised his paddle one final time.","\"Two point eight million.\"","The room fell silent.","The auctioneer glanced toward Sebastian, then brought the gavel down with a crisp smile.","\"Congratulations, Mr. Hale.\"","Sebastian’s face darkened. Alpha Killian had dug into his finances, set the trap, and forced him to pay millions for something Killian had never wanted in the first place.","He scanned the auction room but could not find the private box where Alpha Killian was hiding. His eyes landed on Kate instead.","She only smiled.","Of all the wolves to cross, Alpha Sebastian had picked the young Alpha who always thought three moves ahead.","Today, Alpha Killian had taken his money. Next, he would come for his position and territory.","Call it clever if you were being generous. Ruthless was more accurate.","Eira watched Alpha Killian, quietly impressed by how quickly he had read the situation.","Alpha Killian straightened in his seat. \"Do you have enough left for another bid?\"","\"Yes.\"","A few minutes later, a small antique French mantel clock was brought onto the stage. Its brass details and dark walnut case gave it a classic nineteenth-century look.","The auctioneer opened at $20,000.","Eira’s eyes brightened.","Alpha Killian noticed. \"You want it?\"","She nodded.","He glanced at Natalie. She immediately signaled Kate.","Kate raised her paddle. \"Thirty thousand.\"","No one else dared to compete. The message was clear. Let Sterling have the clock and stay on Alpha Killian’s good side.","A staff member carefully wrapped the clock and carried it up to the private box. Kate handed it to Eira.","\"Nineteenth-century French craftsmanship,\" she said. \"It’s perfect for an old professor. Thoughtful and elegant, but not so flashy that it looks like you’re trying to buy his favor.\"","Eira examined the clock’s brass trim. \"Where do I pay?\"","\"Just settle it with the Alpha. I put it on his card.\"","Eira turned to Alpha Killian. \"Card or bank transfer?\"","Alpha Killian opened his banking app and handed her his phone.","A moment later, the payment went through.","$30,000 transferred.","\"Let’s go, Eira.\"","She was still studying the clock. \"Coming.\"","Downstairs, Alpha Sebastian caught sight of a familiar figure.","\"Eira...\""]},{"number":171,"title":"Chapter 171 A Dangerous Loose End","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian rushed after her, moving too fast to watch where he was going. His thigh slammed into the corner of a table, knocking over an open water bottle. Water spilled down the side and soaked his leather shoes.","A few people turned at the noise.","Alpha Sebastian gritted his teeth, humiliated as much as he was hurt.","\"Alpha, you okay?\"","\"I’m fine.\"","He sent Jordan back to deal with the chair and kept going. By the time he reached the entrance, a black Maybach was already pulling out of the lot.","\"Eira!\"","Only the cold wind and passing headlights answered him.","When Jordan came outside, Alpha Sebastian stood by the curb with his jaw tight. He looked like a wolf that had just lost a scent.","\"Order more burner phones,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"Shut down every number she blocked and keep replacing them.\"","\"Right away, Alpha.\" Jordan hesitated. \"She only blocked your numbers. She hasn’t changed her personal line. That has to mean something. Keep trying. She’ll come around.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression eased slightly. \"You really think so?\"","Jordan nodded. He had no intention of saying otherwise.","The auction staff loaded the antique armchair into the car. Alpha Sebastian reached for the door, then stopped.","\"Alpha?\"","\"You said she never changed her number.\"","His silver-flecked eyes darkened as a memory surfaced.","Two years earlier, he and Eira had visited the Omega shelter where she grew up.","Eira had given her personal number to an autistic pup named Sam.","She kept her phone on around the clock and answered every call from that area, even if the number was blocked.","\"Jordan, fly out tomorrow. Find the boy from that shelter. His name is Sam.\"","If Alpha Sebastian found Sam, Eira would come to him.","--","Dr. Shaw’s birthday dinner was held at a small farmhouse restaurant outside the city. It was the kind of place locals kept to themselves, with no sign out front and no online reservations.","Outside the Shaw family, the only people invited were Eira and Beatrice.","Beatrice had planned to attend, but something came up and she had to stay home. She sent her butler, Martin, to drop off her gift and check in on Eira before dinner.","When Martin saw Eira, his worried expression eased.","\"You look better, Miss Eira,\" he said. \"You’re eating properly, I hope.\"","\"Mrs. Jones is making sure of it. Three meals a day, plenty of fruit, and enough soup to feed a small army. Last night, she spent an hour looking up recipes with medicinal herbs.\"","Martin smiled with relief. \"Good. Beatrice has been worried about you. Let me send her a quick video so she can see you for herself.\"","Eira rarely appeared on social media. When she posted anything, it was usually a research update or a photo of the scenery, never her own face. Still, she stood beside Martin and let him record a short video for Beatrice.","\"Give Beatrice my best,\" Eira said.","\"I will. Take care, Miss Eira.\"","\"You too, Martin.\"","Once Martin had left, Felix finally gathered the courage to approach her. He held out his hand, looking far more nervous than the situation required.","\"Dr. Crawford, it’s a pleasure to meet you.\"","Eira shook his hand. \"You can call me Eira. And I’m sorry I didn’t tell you who I was at the gala.\"","Felix quickly shook his head. \"No, please. You don’t have to apologize. My grandfather would’ve kept your secret anyway.\"","His ears turned red. He was standing in front of the woman his grandfather admired most, and he had already forgotten what he wanted to say.","When he realized he was still holding her hand, he let go at once.","\"Right,\" he said. \"Eira. Welcome.\"","He guided her to the seat beside his grandfather.","Dr. Shaw watched him with open disapproval. \"Useless.\"","Felix laughed. \"I never claimed I could compete with Dr. Crawford.\"","\"Sit down,\" Dr. Shaw ordered.","Everyone took their seats. Felix glanced at the empty chair near the end of the table.","\"Grandpa, are we waiting for someone else?\"","\"Thomas Crawford’s nephew,\" Dr. Shaw said. \"You met him back East.\"","As if summoned by the mention, Vincent Crawford appeared in the doorway with a gift in his hand.","His gaze lifted.","The moment he saw Eira, he stopped.","Eira went still too.The last person she’d expected at Dr. Shaw’s table was Serena’s admirer.","Felix noticed her confusion and leaned closer to explain.","\"It’s a long story,\" he whispered. \"Grandpa and I met Vincent’s uncle at a conference last spring. We were attending an event in his territory, and Grandpa needed a small favor. They stayed in touch afterward. Vincent happens to be in California now, so his uncle asked him to bring Grandpa’s birthday gift.\"","Eira glanced toward the gift in Vincent’s hand. \"And Dr. Shaw invited him to dinner?\"","Felix nodded. \"Exactly. He couldn’t very well turn away someone who’d come all that way to deliver a birthday gift.\"","Eira nodded. \"Got it. Thanks.\"","\"Eira,\" Dr. Shaw called.","She stood at once.","\"This is Vincent Crawford,\" Dr. Shaw said. \"He’s an attorney. And yes, you two have the same last name. No, you’re not related. I checked before I invited him.\"","Vincent smiled. \"I’m a little disappointed. I was hoping for a dramatic family secret.\"","\"Give it time,\" Felix said. \"This family has plenty of those.\"","\"Nice to meet you, Vincent,\" Eira said politely.","\"Nice to meet you, Eira.\"","They exchanged a few brief pleasantries before taking their seats.","Dr. Shaw usually banned business talk at the dinner table. Tonight, he made an exception. Once the plates had been cleared, he turned to Eira.","\"Two companies are trying to get one of my patents. Hale Group is one of them. I haven’t made up my mind yet. What do you think?\"","His expression sharpened.","\"And how are things between you and Sebastian these days?\"","If Eira still had feelings for Alpha Sebastian, Dr. Shaw was prepared to help her walk away.","At the mention of Hale Group, Vincent looked straight at Eira.","She ignored him.","\"Sebastian and I are divorced.\"","Felix’s eyes widened. \"Seriously? Congratulations on escaping, Dr. Crawford.\"","\"Felix,\" Dr. Shaw warned.","Then he looked at Eira. \"You’re not planning to go back to him, are you?\"","\"Never.\"","Her voice left no room for doubt.","Then, making sure Vincent understood exactly why, she added, \"The woman Sebastian truly wants is pregnant.\"","Vincent’s fingers tightened around his glass.","[Serena’s pregnant? Since when? Why didn’t she tell me?]","Dr. Shaw had no interest in Alpha Sebastian’s messy love life. Eira’s answer was all he needed.","\"Give the patent to the other company,\" he told Felix.","\"Done. I’ll call them tomorrow.\""]},{"number":172,"title":"Chapter 172 Doubts Take Root","paragraphs":["After dinner, Eira and Vincent watched Dr. Shaw and the others leave. Once they were alone, Vincent turned to her.","\"You and Sebastian were bonded. Did you really have to wreck his business?\"","Eira turned to face him. \"Are you upset because I cleared the way for Serena, or because I’m making it harder for you to pursue her?\"","Vincent said nothing.","His silence told her everything.","\"You looked pretty shocked when I mentioned the pregnancy,\" Eira said. \"I’m guessing Serena never told you.\"","She picked up her bag.","\"If you think I’m lying, ask her yourself.\"","That was all she needed.","Once Vincent contacted Serena, Eira would know exactly where she was hiding.","Vincent’s polite smile vanished.","\"Serena has already been removed from the Sovereign Processor Initiative,\" he said. \"She lost her position, her credit, and any claim to the project. Why bring up her pregnancy in front of Dr. Shaw?\"","\"Because she earned none of it.\"","Eira’s voice stayed calm.","\"She forced her way in through her grandfather’s connections, tried to replace Professor Davies, and attempted to pass core data to Sebastian so Hale Group could win the bid. Being removed was the least she deserved.\"","Vincent’s gaze hardened. \"You don’t understand how this world works. Power protects power. A lone wolf without a Pack behind her gets crushed.\"","\"Then Serena should have thought about that before she betrayed the project.\"","\"You already have a career and a future. Why keep going after her? She was just another woman Sebastian lied to. If he let her into his bed, he was never loyal to you.\"","Eira gave him a cool look. \"Did I let Sebastian off the hook?\"","Vincent fell silent.","\"You’ve spent the last ten minutes blaming me for damaging his business. Now you want me to protect Serena from the consequences of hers.\"","\"She never meant to come between bonded mates.\"","\"She knew Sebastian was bonded.\"","\"That’s impossible.\"","\"It isn’t.\" Eira’s eyes sharpened. \"And Sebastian funded her for years through his department. If you’re planning to defend her, Counselor, you should start by finding out how much of that money came from marital or Pack assets.\"","Vincent’s expression changed. \"What are you talking about?\"","\"You’re an attorney. Ask Serena.\"","Headlights swept across the lot. Eira checked the license plate of the black Maybach waiting for her.","Vincent stepped closer. \"Eira, if you know something, say it.\"","She opened the car door.","\"Ask her where she’s been hiding. Ask her who paid her bills. Then ask yourself what happens when the court learns she conceived a child with a bonded Alpha during the separation period.\"","Vincent’s face went tight.","Eira slipped into the back seat.","\"If you think I’m lying, call Serena.\"","The door shut.","The Maybach disappeared down the road, leaving Vincent alone under the parking lot lights.","His phone rang. Lainey.","he asked. The sharpness in his voice vanished. \"Did you finish the shoot?\" he asked. The sharpness in his voice vanished.","\"Not yet. I haven’t booked my flight. If you’re still in Palo Alto, I’ll come to you. Mom and Dad said you pulled some strings out West recently. Was it for Serena?\"","Vincent avoided the question. \"I’ll be here for a while. Book your flight and send me the details. I’ll handle the hotel.\"","\"Deal.\"","\"And bring a coat. It’s cold here. If you show up in a tank top, I’m buying you a jacket at the airport.\"","\"Yes, my dear brother.\"","\"I’m serious.\"","\"Then buy me one,Vincent. You know I can’t resist a good coat.\"","\"You girls care more about looking cute than staying warm.\"","He paused before asking, \"Are you still in touch with Serena?\"","\"I called yesterday. She hung up after two minutes. She sounded distracted.\"","Vincent looked toward the road where Eira’s car had vanished.","\"Come tomorrow. Take Serena out for dinner.\"","\"Why me? You’re in the same city. If you want to see her, ask her yourself.\"","\"She’s had a lot going on. We’ll see.\"","They talked for another minute before hanging up.","Once he got home, Vincent dropped onto the couch and stared at his phone for a long moment.","[Are you pregnant?]He typed,","Then deleted it.","Instead, he remembered the first time Serena had helped him.","He remembered following her through unfamiliar streets, laughing as she talked about the work she loved. At twenty-seven, she was the first woman who had ever made him feel truly alive.","Now Eira’s words kept circling back.","Funding.","Was she trying to manipulate him, or had Alpha Sebastian really used Pack and marital money to support Serena? Had Serena known from the beginning that Alpha Sebastian was already bonded?","Vincent opened his messages and typed:","[Serena, Lainey is flying into town tomorrow. Are you free for dinner?]"]},{"number":173,"title":"Chapter 173 Return the Gift","paragraphs":["When Eira got home, Lila was stretched out on the living room rug with her laptop open on the coffee table, completely absorbed in her draft.","Eira started to speak, but Mrs. Jones pressed a finger to her lips.","\"She told me not to interrupt her,\" the housekeeper whispered.","Eira nodded. Interrupting someone in the middle of a thought was the fastest way to ruin their focus. Mrs. Jones brought her a mug of hot honeysuckle tea, and Eira settled behind the couch to drink it quietly while Lila finished editing.","A few minutes later, Lila threw herself onto her back.","\"Finally!\"","Mrs. Jones grinned and tipped her chin toward the couch.","Lila turned. \"Eira, you’re back!\"","She pulled Eira onto the couch and handed her the laptop. \"I made all the changes you suggested. Can you look it over?\"","Eira adjusted her glasses and read through the draft. After a moment, she nodded.","\"Unless Professor Chase finds another problem, you’re ready to submit.\"","\"For real?\" Lila beamed. \"I knew it. I’m brilliant.\"","Eira gave her a faint smile.","Mrs. Jones set a bowl of fresh fruit on the coffee table, and Lila immediately grabbed a strawberry.","\"So, how was Dr. Shaw’s birthday dinner?\" she asked.","\"Fine. I ran into Vincent Crawford.\"","Lila stopped chewing. \"He didn’t give you trouble, did he?\"","\"No. I need to ask you something. Where does your family go when you need someone followed?\"","\"We keep a private security firm on retainer. They handle Pack business, border patrols, tracking rogues, all of it.\" Lila studied her face. \"You want someone watching Vincent?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Ask my brother. He’ll love it.\" She smirked. \"Keeping tabs on a rival Pack’s heir is probably his idea of a relaxing afternoon.\"","\"I’ll cover the cost.\"","\"Then pay Killian directly.\"","Eira pulled out her phone and sent Alpha Killian a text.","His call came seconds later.","Lila and Mrs. Jones exchanged a knowing look. Alpha Killian never called either of them back that fast.","\"Killian,\" Eira answered.","\"You want Vincent watched?\" Alpha Killian asked, his voice low and calm. \"Do you think Serena will run to him, or will he go looking for her?\"","\"Both.\"","\"I’ll put a team on him. Standard rate.\"","\"Thank you.\"","She ended the call, then turned to Mrs. Jones.","\"Could you keep track of the grocery expenses for me?\"","The housekeeper’s eyes gleamed. \"Of course. I can give you a full report at the end of the year. Every receipt, every penny.\"","\"A year is too long. Let’s do it quarterly.\"","\"Deal.\"","--","The Shaw Estate","Dr. Shaw watched Felix carry the gift Eira had brought him into the study.","\"Careful with that,\" he called. \"If you break it, you’re explaining it to her.\"","Felix looked over his shoulder. \"I’m carrying it like it’s made of glass.\"","\"Good. Now get out of my sight.\"","Felix laughed and disappeared into the study.","Dr. Shaw settled into the living room with a glass of bourbon. A few minutes later, the housekeeper appeared in the doorway.","\"Dr. Shaw, someone from Hale Group stopped by earlier.\"","His expression changed. \"Who?\"","\"He said his name was Sebastian Hale. I didn’t let him through the gate. He waited outside for almost an hour before leaving.\"","Dr. Shaw’s fingers tightened around his glass. \"Did he leave anything?\"","\"A chair.\" She hesitated. \"A very expensive one. I had the staff bring it inside.\"","\"Send it back.\"","The housekeeper nodded, but before she could leave, Felix stepped out of the study.","\"Send what back?\"","\"Sebastian left a gift,\" she explained. \"A rosewood armchair.\"","Felix’s face tightened. \"He actually came here?\"","\"He waited at the gate,\" the housekeeper said. \"He wouldn’t leave until I took the chair.\"","Dr. Shaw’s eyes turned cold. \"Return it tomorrow.\"","\"Of course.\"","Felix understood immediately. His grandfather wasn’t upset about the chair.","He was upset because Alpha Sebastian had thrown Eira away.","Felix said, \"Don’t worry, Grandpa. I’ll handle it.\"","--","The next morning, Felix had the armchair delivered to Hale Group.","The receptionist stared at the large wooden crate beside him.","\"Is that a delivery?\" she asked.","\"A return.\"","She looked at the crate, then at Felix. \"Do you have an appointment?\"","\"No. Call Sebastian Hale and tell him Felix Shaw is here.\"","The receptionist’s expression changed at once. She picked up the phone.","A few minutes later, security arrived and escorted Felix upstairs.","On the way up, Felix glanced at the receptionist.","\"How long have you worked here?\"","\"About two years.\"","\"You knew Sebastian was married?\"","She stared at him. \"Married? No. Everyone thinks he’s the most eligible bachelor in the state.\"","\"Everyone?\"","\"Pretty much. There are rumors he’s seeing someone, but no one knows who.\"","Felix gave her a small smile. \"Interesting.\"","The elevator doors opened.","Alpha Sebastian was waiting outside his office. Then he saw the crate.","His expression barely changed, but the polite smile he had prepared disappeared.","\"Felix,\" he said. \"Come in.\"","\"All right.\"","Felix walked into the office and shut the door behind him.","\"You left this at my grandfather’s house last night,\" he said. \"I’m returning it.\"","Alpha Sebastian glanced at the crate.","The words sounded polite, but the message was obvious. Dr. Shaw had rejected the gift.","Maybe he had rejected the patent deal too.","\"That was inappropriate of me,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"I apologize.\"","Felix folded his arms. \"It’s a beautiful chair. My grandfather would have liked it.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s eyes lifted.","\"But he won’t be keeping it.\"","The hope vanished from Alpha Sebastian’s face.","Felix continued, \"My grandfather has spent years talking about Eira. She was the student he valued most, apart from Dr. Thorne. He trusted her judgment.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression shifted.","\"You only got through his door because Eira put in a good word for you,\" Felix said. \"Then you betrayed her.\"","Alpha Sebastian went still. \"Eira introduced me to Dr. Shaw?\"","\"You didn’t know?\"","Alpha Sebastian said nothing.","Felix gave a short, humorless laugh. \"You really never bothered to ask.\"","Alpha Sebastian had always assumed Serena had made the introduction through her grandfather.","It had never occurred to him that Eira had been the reason Dr. Shaw agreed to see him at all.","Now he realized he had been wrong about that too."]},{"number":174,"title":"Chapter 174 Bad Character, No Deal","paragraphs":["Felix took one look at Alpha Sebastian’s face and let out a quiet laugh.","\"You really thought Serena got you in?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression barely changed, but his hand tightened around the edge of the desk.","\"Looks like she let you believe that.\" Felix folded his arms. \"My grandfather doesn’t do favors for the Winthrops. He and Dr. Winthrop can barely sit through the same dinner.\"","Alpha Sebastian said nothing.","\"Rival labs. Old grudges.\" Felix shrugged. \"If Dr. Winthrop had actually recommended you, you’d be even farther from getting a deal.\"","Something shifted in the room.","The truth finally registered on Alpha Sebastian’s face.","Dr. Shaw had opened his door because of Eira.","Not Serena.","Eira.","\"Whatever you thought you got from her, you didn’t earn it,\" Felix said. \"Eira did everything she could to keep your Pack and your company standing, and you betrayed her.\"","He tapped the wooden crate with his shoe.","\"My grandfather’s exact words were, ’Bad character. No deal.’\"","Alpha Sebastian moved toward the door.","\"Name your price.\"","Felix stared at him.","\"I’ll beat whatever the other company offered.\"","\"No.\"","\"I’ll walk away from the project. You can choose the team. I won’t touch the patent.\"","\"You’re still not listening.\"","Felix’s voice stayed flat.","\"He doesn’t trust you.\"","A knock sounded at the door.","Finn leaned against the open doorway, his hair still messed up from sleep.","\"You called me?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s face went blank.","\"I crashed in the break room,\" Finn added. \"What did I miss?\"","\"Nothing.\"","Felix walked past Alpha Sebastian. His men followed, pushing the crate down the hall.","Finn watched them leave.","\"That didn’t look like nothing.\"","\"Go back to sleep.\"","\"We’re supposed to review the Shaw proposal today.\"","\"Then review it again.\"","Finn frowned at him. \"Seriously. Is something going on?\"","He had caught the tension in Alpha Sebastian’s face.","\"Nothing for now,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"I’m busy.\"","Finn studied him for another second, then shrugged and turned away.","At the doorway, he stopped.","\"Hey, Sebastian. Why don’t you just divorce Eira?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s hand tightened around the doorframe. His smile disappeared.","\"Finn, it’s still business hours.\"","\"Then call it a coffee break.\" Finn turned back, his expression serious. \"You want someone else. Let Eira go. You may not see what she’s worth, but plenty of people do.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened.","First Killian Sterling. Now Finn Carter. Both of them circling his mate like she was unclaimed territory.","\"Eira and I are fine,\" he said. \"We love each other.\"","\"Could’ve fooled me. I heard she hasn’t seen you in weeks.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s pupils contracted.","How did Finn know?","Alpha Sebastian had created two fake accounts, one under Finn’s name and one under Eira’s. Every message between them passed through him first. He controlled what each of them saw.","Unless Finn and Eira had met in person.","Then he remembered Fiona. His sister had probably told Finn everything.","Finn caught the silence in his face.\"So it’s true.\"","Alpha Sebastian said nothing.","Finn’s shoulders relaxed. \"Take it easy. Divorcing Eira won’t cost you your seat at Carter Group. Most people don’t even know you’re bonded. My father has known for years. He knows about the cheating too, and he’s never said a word.\"","Alpha Sebastian swallowed his anger.","\"You want to chase Eira?\" he said. \"Try getting her to sit down with you first.\"","He could not get near her home on Southridge. Eira had blocked every way he could reach her. But if Finn managed to arrange a meeting, there might still be a chance to reopen the Shaw deal.","So Alpha Sebastian went for the weak spot.","\"You can’t even get her to look at you. She’s probably forgotten what you look like. Four years with me, and she never once looked at another man.\"","Finn’s eyes reddened.\"You know she loved you. That’s what makes this so disgusting. You didn’t want her, but you couldn’t stand anyone else wanting her either.\"","He pointed at Alpha Sebastian.\"This is going to come back on you. You’re going to lose her.\"","Finn held his stare for another second, then shook his head.He turned and walked out.","The door slammed behind him.","[You’re going to lose her.]","The words followed Alpha Sebastian all day.","By nightfall, he was still alone in his office. The tower had gone dark around him when a key jammed under his fingers.","He snapped.","With one sweep of his arm, he knocked the keyboard onto the floor.","\"I am not going to lose her,\" he growled at the empty room.","Then the memory came back.","Eira had stood there without blinking while his own housekeeper shoved a mop into his mouth. Her blue eyes had been cold and empty.","She had not looked angry.","She had looked finished with him.","The stench rose in his throat.","Alpha Sebastian barely made it to the sink before he started vomiting."]},{"number":175,"title":"Chapter 175 Half a Breath Away","paragraphs":["Isabella couldn’t let it go.","So what if Serena was carrying her brother’s pup? That should have had nothing to do with her. The money was another story.","She had never seen a hundred million dollars in her life. The thought of losing her share kept her awake at night.","Twice, she had tried to sneak away and make a deal with Eira. Twice, Luna Margaret had caught her by the collar.","\"Don’t think I can’t read that look on your face,\" Luna Margaret snapped. \"Serena is carrying your brother’s heir. Stop stirring the pot.\"","\"How do you know the baby is his?\" Isabella shot back. \"There are always men coming and going around Serena. That guy from the cruise is one example.\"","Luna Margaret’s expression tightened.","Isabella pressed on. \"Who says the baby belongs to Sebastian? She’ll sleep with a young, high-profile Alpha. Why couldn’t she sleep with a Pack elder twice her age?\"","Luna Margaret hated that the argument made sense.","\"Your brother isn’t stupid,\" she said. \"He accepted the pregnancy report without a fight. The baby is his.\"","\"And if it isn’t?\" Isabella gripped the plane ticket she had stolen the last time. \"Then we lose everything. Mom, stop blocking me. I’m getting my share.\"","This time, Luna Margaret let her go.","Isabella went straight to the Silix Institute. Security noticed her within minutes. After questioning her, the guards decided she was too clueless to take pictures of classified technology and let her leave.","She searched for Eira online and found a press release on the Sterling Group website.","Then she headed straight there.","She had barely started loitering near the entrance when two security guards took her down onto the pavement.","\"Eira!\" Isabella screamed. \"Eira, get out here!\"","It worked.","Eira stepped outside in a white lab coat, pulling off her mask.","The guards released Isabella. She brushed the dirt from her clothes and lifted her chin.","\"See? I told you I know her!\"","Eira glanced at the guards. \"If she starts yelling again, put her back on the ground.\"","\"Yes, ma’am.\"","\"Eira, don’t be like that. We’re on the same side.\"","\"I don’t have time for this.\" Eira looked at the ticket in Isabella’s hand. \"What do you want?\"","Isabella held it out.","\"Here.\"","Eira did not take it. \"This is worthless to me.\"","\"Then what do you want?\"","Eira stepped closer.","The cold look in her eyes made Isabella swallow and take a step back.","\"W-What are you doing?\"","\"You know Serena is pregnant?\"","Eira watched her face carefully.","The shock that flashed across Isabella’s expression told Eira everything she needed to know.","\"Get me Serena’s prenatal records,\" Eira said. \"Or arrange for her to be tested at a clinic I choose.\"","Isabella stared at her. \"You want me to steal medical records?\"","\"So you do have a conscience.\"","Eira’s gaze turned dismissive.","\"I’ll give you thirty percent of the marital assets. That’s at least thirty million dollars.\"","\"Deal!\"","Isabella reached out for a high five.","A cold voice cut across the courtyard.","\"What the hell are you doing?\"","Alpha Killian was already striding toward them, his silver-gray eyes fixed on Isabella. He gave the guards one sharp look.","They moved immediately.","Before Isabella could say another word, they grabbed her and pulled her away.","Alpha Killian stopped in front of Eira, his brows drawn tight. The warning presence of an angry Alpha rolled off him, making the air feel colder.","\"Did she touch you?\"","A strange warmth stirred in Eira’s chest. It disappeared before she could figure out what it meant.","\"She came to offer me a deal,\" Eira said. \"That’s all.\"","\"What kind of deal could she possibly...\"","Alpha Killian stopped when he saw that Eira was unharmed. The tension left his jaw, but his eyes stayed cold.","He turned to Kate and Natalie, who had hurried over after hearing that a Hale woman was causing trouble on Sterling property.","\"Any word from the team?\" he asked.","\"Airport pickup confirmed,\" Kate said.","Natalie checked her phone. \"Lainey Crawford just landed.\"","She gave Alpha Killian a pointed look, then glanced at Eira.","Lainey was the last of Alpha Killian’s admirers who still refused to take a hint. Every few weeks, she sent him a text.","Alpha Killian never answered. He simply handed the phone to Natalie, who replied with a sweet voice message about him being tied up in meetings.","Lainey always accepted the excuse. She had never crossed the line far enough for Alpha Killian to block her without turning it into a family issue. Seraphina had already warned him not to make things ugly with the Crawfords.","As if on cue, Natalie’s phone buzzed again.","She looked down at the screen.","[Killian, I’m in town.]","Natalie pulled out the Sterling work phone and typed a reply.","[Hi, Lainey. Alpha Killian is booked solid today. I’ll let him know you reached out.]","She showed the message to Kate. \"Too obvious?\"","Kate read it and gave her a thumbs-up. \"She’ll buy it.\"","Eira looked from one woman to the other. \"What’s going on?\"","\"Lainey Crawford,\" Natalie explained. \"She texts Alpha every time she’s in town. He never answers, so I do.\"","Kate glanced at Eira. \"You’re in his personal contacts too, Dr. Crawford. Welcome to the club.\"","Eira nodded. \"Good. Corporate drones have to stick together.\"","A few steps ahead, Alpha Killian stopped and looked back.","His expression was colder than the mountain wind.","Kate and Natalie lowered their heads and started walking faster.","Natalie made it three steps before turning around. \"The team tracked Serena and Vincent to an old apartment complex near the university. I just sent the address to your phone, Alpha.\"","Then she hurried after Kate, mouthing Bye to Eira.","Eira gave her a small wave.","Alpha Killian pulled up the location on his phone.","\"Do you think they’re going to Serena?\" Eira asked.","He zoomed in on the map. \"Most likely. She’s probably staying with her parents.\"","\"Let me see.\"","Eira stepped closer. Her hair fell loose around her face. The ends grazed his wrist and slid across his palm.","Alpha Killian caught a few strands before they could fall. He ran them once between his fingers, then let them go.","A clean, herbal scent lingered in the air. He recognized it from one of Barry’s old remedies.","Mrs. Jones must have started giving it to Eira.","Alpha Killian looked up.","Eira turned at the same moment.","They stood inches apart, their breath mixing in the cold air.","For one suspended second, Alpha Killian forgot to breathe.","Eira was like a drug, the kind he could get hooked on anywhere, anytime."]}]);
